{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n '\"'^##|''^###'\"' vendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md vendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/docs/ASSETS.md && rg -n '\"'^##|''^###|Platformer|PlatformMap|Attack|Humanoid|pose|registerHat|registerWeapon|allowJoin|input.label'\"' vendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md | head -100\"","aggregated_output":"vendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/docs/ASSETS.md:9:## Use one\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/docs/ASSETS.md:34:## The core library\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/docs/ASSETS.md:46:## Materials on surfaces\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/docs/ASSETS.md:84:## Write one\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/docs/ASSETS.md:116:### Worked entries\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/docs/ASSETS.md:135:## Make one: the recipe\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/docs/ASSETS.md:155:## Limits\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:7:## North star\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:17:## The mental model\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:29:## Remake workflow (port, remaster, reimagine, remix)\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:44:## Visual craft: aim for PS1 / N64 era 2D, not NES\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:64:## Animation: fluid, varied, readable\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:72:## Hard rules\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:82:## Standard features (built in: adjust them, don't rebuild them)\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:120:## Frame order\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:140:## Systems in more depth\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:142:### Views and resolution\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:150:### Scenes\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:155:### Camera\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:163:### Players (two to four on one machine)\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:169:### Motion and timing (tweens, scripts, paths)\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:178:### TileMap (ground-plane levels)\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:190:### Heights: roofs, ledges, sight and reach\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:222:### PlatformMap (side-scrolling levels)\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:242:### Platformer (side-scroller controller)\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:249:### Body (ground-plane physics)\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:255:### Mover and actions (third-person ground controller)\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:267:### Perception (sight, hearing, suspicion)\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:273:### Attack (melee timing)\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:280:### Bullets and patterns\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:286:### Humanoid\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:297:### Audio\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:305:### Text and UI\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:311:### Shell (an HTML interface: screens and HUD)\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:319:### Lighting\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:328:### Errors and warnings\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:338:### Testing without a browser\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:357:### The handoff package\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:360:### Modules (general systems in files of their own)\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:367:### Kits and the diet (which file for which game)\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:374:### Recorded sessions (a bug from a phone, replayed exactly)\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:402:## Genre recipes\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:606:## Building a big game: lessons from Emberdeep\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:631:## Where to find more: animation and examples\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:648:## Performance\nvendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md:656:## Checklist before handing a game back\n5:## Units and the height rules\n22:## Examples\n34:game.dispose();\n47:## Contents\n49:The line each section starts on, and the name its classes' instances go by: `E.Attack: slash` lists its members as `slash.start`.\n69:- 648 Humanoid rig; E.Attack: slash, E.Combo: combo, E.Humanoid: rig\n75:- 861 Platform map; E.PlatformMap: level\n76:- 895 Platformer; E.Platformer: hero\n108:## The engine object (E = My3D2dge)\n119:## 1. Math\n121:- `E.HEIGHTS: eye, chest, level, step`: the numbers of THE HEIGHT RULES, which collision, standing, sight, reach, navigation and drawing all read (API.md, \"Heights\", and the API index's head give the  [... omitted end of long line]\n173:- `E.overlapBox(a, b)`: side-view boxes: { x (center), z (feet), w, h } (the Platformer / PlatformMap convention)\n195:## 2. Pixel primitives\n214:## 2b. Sprite frames, turns and swaps\n220:## 3. Views (projections)\n247:## 4. Screen\n269:## 5. Input\n271:- `new E.Input(screen, map, signal) → input`: signal: an AbortSignal that removes every listener this adds (game.dispose()). A screen without a canvas (headless) gets no DOM listeners: input comes fro [... omitted end of long line]\n293:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), wit [... omitted end of long line]\n357:## 6. Pixel fonts\n368:## 7. Lighting\n384:- `game.lights.screen = false` †: true measures lights on the screen, not the ground (side views and PlatformMaps do it by themselves)\n387:## 8. Particles\n407:## 9. Renderer\n457:## 10. Game\n479:- `game.allowJoin(o = {})` †: let players join, up to max (2..4): Start on a gamepad no one holds, or 2 on the keyboard (o.keys: false not); onJoin (input, number) as each does. allowJoin(false) close [... omitted end of long line]\n482:- `game.dispose()`: end the game for good: stop the loop and remove everything the engine added to the page (its listeners on the window, the document, the canvas and the buttons, the touch controls,  [... omitted end of long line]\n499:- `game.players` †: the players: [game.input (player 1), ...the ones who joined (game.allowJoin, game.addPlayer: section 10j)]; each an input with player (1..4), name ('P1'), color (E.PLAYER_COLORS) a [... omitted end of long line]\n529:- `game.disposed = true`: true after dispose()\n572:## 10b. Standard features\n589:## 10c. Boot\n594:## 10d. Tweens and scripts\n611:## 10e. Paths\n621:## 10g. Weather\n625:## 10k. Save slots\n648:## 11. Humanoid rig\n650:- `new E.Attack(spec = {}, over) → slash`: new E.Attack(spec) or new E.Attack('slash', { reach: 9 }): a name from E.MOVES plus overrides\n656:- `slash.state`: what Humanoid.update wants as `attack` (null when idle)\n663:- `new E.Combo(specs, o = {}) → combo`: new E.Combo(items, { window: .3 }): items are move names, specs or Attacks\n667:- `combo.current`: the Attack of the current hit\n670:- `combo.state`: what Humanoid.update wants as `attack` (null when idle)\n671:- `combo.update(dt)`: advance the current hit; returns the phase that began, as Attack.update\n673:- `combo.moves`: the Attacks\n676:- `new E.Humanoid(o = {}) → rig`: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build, weapon, outfit, hair, hat, sleeves, armor, hood, cape, colors, ... }): a character rig posed from math every step (API.md, \"Charact [... omitted end of long line]\n677:- `E.Humanoid.hat(id, draw)` †: a hat of the game's own: draw(h) with h.at(forward, right, up) a point round the head on screen, h.r its radius there, h.c its color (o.hat.color), h.dk a darker one, h [... omitted end of long line]\n678:- `E.Humanoid.hats` †: the hats a Humanoid may wear, by id: the built-ins (cap, band, crown, helmet, pointed) and a game's own\n679:- `E.Humanoid.pose(id, fn)` †: a held pose of the game's own: fn(J, w, rig) moves the joints (the rig's frame: forward, right, up) toward the pose by w, 0..1, which eases in and out as state.pose name [... omitted end of long line]\n680:- `E.Humanoid.poses` †: the held poses of a game's own, by id (the built-in poses are the rig's own solve: state.pose names either)\n681:- `E.Humanoid.weapon(id, spec)` †: a weapon of the game's own (or a built-in replaced): { length: the tip's distance from the hand (a number, or rig => one; tip() and the swing's trail), rest: [forwar [... omitted end of long line]\n682:- `E.Humanoid.weapons` †: the weapons a Humanoid may hold, by id: the built-ins (sword, gun, staff) and a game's own\n685:- `rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, size = 40, o = {})` †: a close-up bust for dialog boxes and menus, drawn live from the rig (blinks, hair and hats included): rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, 40, { zoom: 3, turn: [... omitted end of long line]\n693:- `rig.update(dt, s = {})`: s: { x, y, z, vx, vy, facing, dash, hurt, attack, air, point } air: true while jumping or falling (legs tuck), point: true to hold the weapon hand forward (aiming a gun) at [... omitted end of long line]\n701:- `rig.dieT`: pose 'die': a stagger, the knees give, then the body topples\n702:- `rig.downW`: how far down it is, 0..1 (state down, pose 'down' or 'die'): it falls faster and faster and gets up steadily\n711:- `rig.poseW`: held poses: 'cheer' (item get, victory), 'cast' (both hands forward), 'guard' (fists up), 'kneel', 'crouch', 'wave', 'hips' (hands on hips), and down: 0..1 (knocked flat). stance: 'guar [... omitted end of long line]\n719:- `E.MOVES: slash, backslash, overhead, rising, thrust, spin, plunge, twohand, jab, cross, hook, uppercut, haymaker, elbow, ... (24)`: a library of named attacks with timing and body motion (anticipat [... omitted end of long line]\n727:## 12. Blob rig\n747:## 13. Tile map\n811:## 13b. Materials\n832:## 14. Flow field\n850:## 15. Texture helpers for floortex functions\n861:## 16. Platform map\n863:- `new E.PlatformMap(o = {}) → level`: { rows: [...ASCII, top row first...], legend: { '#': 1, '@': 'hero' }, types: { 1: {...} }, tile: 16, depth: 16 }. Tile kinds: 'solid' (default) | 'oneway' | 'la [... omitted end of long line]\n895:## 16b. Platformer\n897:- `new E.Platformer(o = {}) → hero`: a side-scroller character body with modern, forgiving controls (coyote time, jump buffering, variable jump height, optional double jump, wall jump, dash, ladders,  [... omitted end of long line]\n900:- `hero.rigState(extra)`: state for Humanoid.update: rig.update(dt, hero.rigState({ attack }))\n936:## 17. Body\n956:## 17b. Actions\n964:- `action.rigState(extra)` †: the rig state for the body (merge extra over it): x, y, z, its speed, facing and the beat's pose\n978:## 17c. Mover\n984:- `mover.rigState(extra)` †: the rig state: rig.update(dt, hero.rigState({ attack })): its motion, crouch, sprint and landing, or the playing action's pose; extra is merged over it\n1017:## 17d. Perception\n1019:- `new E.Suspicion(o = {}) → suspicion`: new E.Suspicion({ rise, decay, notice, search, alert, forget }): a guard's mind (its fields, below, are its options). Its level rises while it sees the target  [... omitted end of long line]\n1034:## 18. Bullets\n1042:- `shots.update(dt, map)`: move them one step; with a map they stop at walls (a TileMap, or a PlatformMap in side views)\n1054:## 19. Spatial hash\n1064:## 20. Audio\n1098:## 21b. Backdrops\n1106:## 21c. Props\n1111:## 21e. Shapes\n1123:## 21. Ui\n1130:- `talk.say(text, o = {})`: open with one string or a list of strings (each starts a new page). opts: { name, onDone, choices, onChoice, portrait: rig (a live close-up of that Humanoid beside the text [... omitted end of long line]\n1149:- `talk.portrait`: the portrait beside the text (a Humanoid, or a function (g, x, y, size)), or null; pSize: its size in pixels; pOpts: its options ({ zoom, turn, bg })\n1184:## 21d. Shell\n1193:- `shell.dispose()` †: take its elements away and let go of the game (game.dispose() does it)\n1213:## 22. Gpu lighting (webgpu)\n1234:## 23. Sessions\n1243:## Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js)\n1278:## Module click: point-and-click adventures: walk areas with holes, depth, hotspots, verbs, an inventory (engine/modules/click.js)\n1323:## Module drive: cars on the ground plane, a race round a track, the drivers who race it (engine/modules/drive.js)\n1361:## Module fight: one-on-one fighting: fighters with frame data, guards, throws, specials, a meter; rounds; a CPU; training (engine/modules/fight.js)\n1387:- `new E.Fighter(game, o = {}) → fighter` †: new E.Fighter(game, { name, x, side: 1 (faces right), rig: Humanoid options (or a Humanoid), life: 1000, walk: 75, back: 60, jump: 390, jumpX: 90, moves, t [... omitted end of long line]\n1399:- `fighter.body` †: its E.Platformer (x, z: its feet; w, h: its push box)\n1415:- `fighter.moves` †: { id: spec }, each spec with its E.Attack (atk) and its frame data (frames: [startup, active, recovery])\n1418:- `fighter.rig` †: its E.Humanoid (drawn and posed from its state every step)\n1423:- `fighter.win = false` †: in its win pose\n1442:## Module gen: generated maps: rooms and corridors, BSP, caves, mazes and scatter, from a seed (engine/modules/gen.js)\n1453:## Module grid: square and hex grids: paths, ranges, lines, fields of view, fog, groups, movers and turns (engine/modules/grid.js)\n1512:## Module mode7: a perspective floor drawn a row at a time, a sky that turns with it, everything on it scaled by its distance (engine/modules/mode7.js)\n1535:## Module physics: 2D rigid bodies: circles, boxes, polygons, segments; fast balls that never pass through (engine/modules/physics.js)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
