{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '6307,6420p' vendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js && sed -n '6722,6970p' vendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '648,719p' vendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md && sed -n '269,313p' vendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md && sed -n '195,214p' vendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md\"","aggregated_output":"## 11. Humanoid rig\n\n- `new E.Attack(spec = {}, over) → slash`: new E.Attack(spec) or new E.Attack('slash', { reach: 9 }): a name from E.MOVES plus overrides\n- `slash.active`: true while the strike can connect\n- `slash.busy`: true from the wind-up to the end of the recovery\n- `slash.cancel()`: stop the swing at once (hurt, dodged into)\n- `slash.hits(targets, test, fn)`: during 'active', call fn(target) once per swing for each target where test(target) is true. Returns how many were hit\n- `slash.start(canCancel = false)`: begin a swing if idle (or when canCancel and already recovering). Returns true if it started\n- `slash.state`: what Humanoid.update wants as `attack` (null when idle)\n- `slash.u`: 0..1 progress through the current phase\n- `slash.update(dt)`: advance the swing by dt seconds; returns the phase that began during it ('active' = play the swing sound), or null\n- `slash.hit`: the targets this swing has hit (each is hit once)\n- `slash.phase = null`: 'wind' | 'active' | 'recover', or null when idle\n- `slash.spec`: the move: seconds of wind, active and recover, and its shape for the rig (a0, a1, z0, z1, reach, hitAt)\n- `slash.t = 0`: seconds into the phase\n- `new E.Combo(specs, o = {}) → combo`: new E.Combo(items, { window: .3 }): items are move names, specs or Attacks\n- `combo.active`: true while the current hit can connect\n- `combo.busy`: true while a hit of the chain is swinging\n- `combo.cancel()`: stop the chain; the next press starts it over\n- `combo.current`: the Attack of the current hit\n- `combo.hits(targets, test, fn)`: the current hit's hits(targets, test, fn): fn(target) once per swing where test(target) is true\n- `combo.press()`: start or continue the chain. Returns true if a hit started\n- `combo.state`: what Humanoid.update wants as `attack` (null when idle)\n- `combo.update(dt)`: advance the current hit; returns the phase that began, as Attack.update\n- `combo.idle = 99`: seconds since the last hit ended\n- `combo.moves`: the Attacks\n- `combo.step = -1`: the index of the current hit (-1 before the first)\n- `combo.window`: seconds after a hit ends that a press still chains\n- `new E.Humanoid(o = {}) → rig`: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build, weapon, outfit, hair, hat, sleeves, armor, hood, cape, colors, ... }): a character rig posed from math every step (API.md, \"Characters\", lists the options); update(dt, state) each step, draw(g, ox, oy, view) inside r.actor. hat: 'cap' | 'band' | 'crown' | 'helmet' | 'pointed' (or { style, color }; E.Humanoid.hat adds one); weapon: 'sword' | 'gun' | 'staff' (E.Humanoid.weapon adds one); hood: true (drawn in colors.hair); draw: { under(g, Q, rig), over(g, Q, rig) } the game's own drawing before and after the body (Q: the joints on screen, [x, y, depth]: outfits, accessories); seed: its own random stream (blinks, its clock)\n- `E.Humanoid.hat(id, draw)` †: a hat of the game's own: draw(h) with h.at(forward, right, up) a point round the head on screen, h.r its radius there, h.c its color (o.hat.color), h.dk a darker one, h.g, h.rig\n- `E.Humanoid.hats` †: the hats a Humanoid may wear, by id: the built-ins (cap, band, crown, helmet, pointed) and a game's own\n- `E.Humanoid.pose(id, fn)` †: a held pose of the game's own: fn(J, w, rig) moves the joints (the rig's frame: forward, right, up) toward the pose by w, 0..1, which eases in and out as state.pose names it or not (blended over the rig's solve)\n- `E.Humanoid.poses` †: the held poses of a game's own, by id (the built-in poses are the rig's own solve: state.pose names either)\n- `E.Humanoid.weapon(id, spec)` †: a weapon of the game's own (or a built-in replaced): { length: the tip's distance from the hand (a number, or rig => one; tip() and the swing's trail), rest: [forward, right, up] the way it points held at rest, blade: true (a swing smears along it), draw(w): its drawing in both styles (w.style, w.at(t), w.push(depth, fn), w.u: rig._weaponDraw) }\n- `E.Humanoid.weapons` †: the weapons a Humanoid may hold, by id: the built-ins (sword, gun, staff) and a game's own\n- `rig.debug(r)` †: skeleton overlay for debugging, draws straight into the buffer\n- `rig.draw(g, ox, oy, view)`: draw into g with (ox, oy) = projected position of the rig's root\n- `rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, size = 40, o = {})` †: a close-up bust for dialog boxes and menus, drawn live from the rig (blinks, hair and hats included): rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, 40, { zoom: 3, turn: .6, bg: '#1a2050', frame: true }) // inside r.overlay(g => ...) zoom: pixels per world unit (3 = face fills the frame), turn: 0 = facing you, .6 = three-quarter. The bust stays upright while the rig kneels or lies down (upright: false shows the real pose); cape: false hides the cape; tint: '#808080' greys it out (a KO'd party member).\n- `rig.drawSmear(r, colors = ['#ffffff', '#dff8ff', '#8fe0f2', '#4bb1d4'])` †: motion smear for the current swing, queued in front of the rig\n- `rig.hand(which = 'R')`: world position of a hand ('R' holds the weapon): spawn bullets, sparks or thrown things here\n- `rig.head()`: world position of the head (for speech bubbles, portraits, halos)\n- `rig.kick(v)`: a squash-and-stretch kick: + stretches (a jump), - squashes (a landing, a hit)\n- `rig.land(strength = 1)` †: a heavy landing: knees bend deep and spring back over a moment; strength 1 or more drops a hand to the ground (a three-point landing), .3-.6 is a soft one. Call it on the step the body lands\n- `rig.solvePose()`: set the joints J from the rig's state this step (update and setPose call it); a clip player may wrap it on one rig: const base = rig.solvePose; rig.solvePose = function () { base.call(this); ...move J... }\n- `rig.tip()`: world position of the weapon tip (sword tip, gun muzzle, staff orb)\n- `rig.update(dt, s = {})`: s: { x, y, z, vx, vy, facing, dash, hurt, attack, air, point } air: true while jumping or falling (legs tuck), point: true to hold the weapon hand forward (aiming a gun) attack: { spec, phase: 'wind' | 'active' | 'recover', u: 0..1 }. spec.kick = true swings the right foot instead of the hand also aim (radians up), crouch, sprint, climb, hang (hangZ: the top it hangs from, above the feet), flip: 0..1 (a roll), pose: 'cheer' | 'cast' | 'guard' | 'kneel' | 'crouch' | 'wave' | 'hips' | 'down' | 'die' | 'block' or one of E.Humanoid.pose's, tilt (radians: the whole body forward about the feet, a dive) and roll (sideways), stance: 'guard' | 'ready', down: 0..1, vz (with climb: the climbing speed), land: k (a heavy landing), expr: 'smile' | 'shout' | 'angry' | 'wince', run: 0..1 (run in place)\n- `rig.worldOffset(p)`: where a point in the rig's own frame ([forward, right, up]; a joint such as rig.J.head, or one offset from it) sits, in world units from the rig's feet: add rig.x, y, z for the world point, or project it to draw at a joint\n- `rig.C`: its colors (skin, hair, cloth, pants, boot, belt, cape, capeIn, metal, hilt, eye, ...), the defaults with o.colors over them; change one and it shows at the next draw\n- `rig.J`: its joints this step in its own frame ({ hipL, kneeL, footL, shC, head, handR, ... }; rig.worldOffset(J.handR) gives one in the world)\n- `rig.atkZ = 10`: the height of the weapon hand during an attack\n- `rig.blink = 2`: seconds to the next blink\n- `rig.capeL = null`: the cape's left edge points (null until it has a cape and has moved)\n- `rig.capeR = []`: the cape's right edge points\n- `rig.dieT`: pose 'die': a stagger, the knees give, then the body topples\n- `rig.downW`: how far down it is, 0..1 (state down, pose 'down' or 'die'): it falls faster and faster and gets up steadily\n- `rig.expr` †: the face shown ('smile', 'shout', 'angry', 'wince'), or null\n- `rig.facing = 0`: the angle it faces, radians\n- `rig.hop`: how high an attack's hop lifts it now\n- `rig.hurtW = 0`: 0..1, how far into the hurt flinch\n- `rig.lastView` †: drawSmear projects the trail with the same view\n- `rig.lunge`: how far the body leans into an attack now, world units\n- `rig.o`: its options, with the build's proportions and the defaults filled in (size, build, weapon, outfit, ...; legUpper, torso, headR and the other lengths are at size 1)\n- `rig.phase = 0`: the walk cycle's phase, radians\n- `rig.poseW`: held poses: 'cheer' (item get, victory), 'cast' (both hands forward), 'guard' (fists up), 'kneel', 'crouch', 'wave', 'hips' (hands on hips), and down: 0..1 (knocked flat). stance: 'guard' (fists up while moving) | 'ready' (weapon held forward)\n- `rig.reach = 7`: how far it reaches forward\n- `rig.spin = 0`: the body's extra turn during a spinning move, radians\n- `rig.sq = 0`: squash and stretch, -0.45..0.45 (kick adds to it)\n- `rig.sqV = 0`: its speed\n- `rig.t`: seconds of its own clock (idle breathing, blinks)\n- `rig.trail = []` †: recent points of the blade (or fist) tip, for the swing's smear\n- `rig.x = 0`, `rig.y = 0`, `rig.z = 0`: where its feet are (from the last update)\n- `E.MOVES: slash, backslash, overhead, rising, thrust, spin, plunge, twohand, jab, cross, hook, uppercut, haymaker, elbow, ... (24)`: a library of named attacks with timing and body motion (anticipation, lunge, step, twist, hop). new E.Attack('overhead'), new E.Attack('thrust', { reach: 10 }), new E.Combo(['jab', 'cross', 'hook', 'uppercut']) rig.update(dt, { ..., attack: E.move('roundhouse', .5) }) // any move at any moment, for previews and cutscenes The same move works on every build and in every view: heights are relative to the shoulders (rel: true), reaches scale with arm length, and horizontal swings turn into screen-plane swings in side views. A move's spec fields:\n## 5. Input\n\n- `new E.Input(screen, map, signal) → input`: signal: an AbortSignal that removes every listener this adds (game.dispose()). A screen without a canvas (headless) gets no DOM listeners: input comes from press(code), release(code), tap(action) and hold(action, on)\n- `E.Input.DEFAULT { attack, dash, skill, jump }`: top-down / isometric action (Zelda, Diablo): Space dashes, J or click attacks\n- `E.Input.PLATFORMER { jump, attack, dash, skill }`: side-scrollers (Mario, Mega Man): Space / Z / K jump, X / J attack or shoot, Shift / C dash\n- `E.Input.SHMUP { fire, bomb }`: shoot-'em-ups (1942, Gradius): Space / Z / J fire (hold for autofire), X / K bomb\n- `E.Input.THIRDPERSON { sprint, jump, crouch, interact, attack, block, dodge, use, map }` †: third-person action and stealth (Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear): WASD / stick move, Shift sprint, Space jump and parkour, C crouch (a toggle), E interact, J attack, K block, L dodge, Q use, M map. Pad: A jump, B crouch, X attack, Y interact, LB block, RB dodge, LT use, RT or L3 sprint, Back map\n- `E.Input.halfKeys(preset, side)` †: a preset for half a keyboard ('left' or 'right'): its moves and menu keys, the preset's other actions on its buttons in order, and the preset's gamepad codes (Input.halfKeys(Input.SHMUP, 'right') -> fire on . and Numpad 1, bomb on /). A preset's own halves come first: preset.halves = { left: { pass: ['KeyR'] }, right: { pass: ['KeyL'] } } (an action a menu reads beside confirm would take confirm's F otherwise)\n- `input.anyPressed()`: any action pressed this step (title screens: \"press any button\")\n- `input.bindButtons(root)` †: wire every element with data-act=\"<action>\" inside root to the action\n- `input.bindings` †: the player's bindings over the preset: { action: { keys: [codes], pad: [codes] } } (game.settings.bindings keeps them)\n- `input.box()` †: the pointer's gestures, read each step in screen pixels (the HUD's space), from a mouse or one finger: box() -> { x0, y0, x1, y1, from, to, done } while a box is drawn (a mouse's left button dragged; on a touch screen a long press, then a drag), done the step it is let go; else null\n- `input.buffered(a, win = .15)`: was it pressed within the last `win` seconds and not yet consumed? (input buffering)\n- `input.clear()`: Release all devices and discard buffered input on focus loss or a modal transition.\n- `input.clicked()` †: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step after it lifted (a press that drags away, like the touch stick's, is none); else null. Menus and dialogs answer to it; a HUD button of your own can: if (hit(input.clicked())) ...\n- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n- `input.consume(a)`: mark a buffered press of action a as used, so buffered(a) is false until the next press\n- `input.consumeAll()`: forget every pending press (after closing a menu or dialog, so the same press does not also attack)\n- `input.doubleTap()` †: [x, y] the step a second tap or click lands within .35 s and 8 pixels of the first (a double tap), else null\n- `input.down(a)`: is the action held right now?\n- `input.drag()` †: how far the touch stick's finger moved since the last step, in screen pixels [dx, dy] (the HUD's space), or null while no finger holds it: to steer one to one (a shooter's ship follows the thumb) instead of by the stick's direction\n- `input.feed(type, x, y, o = {})` †: a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false, button: 0, id: 0 (which finger, for zones) }) (a test's or a bot's mouse and fingers: clicks, boxes, long presses, double taps and pans follow; a finger in one of the zones holds its act), or feed('zoom', x, y, { k: 1.1 }): a wheel's notch or a pinch about that point\n- `input.history` †: the last second of input, oldest first: [{ t (input.clock), dir (numpad 1-9 for a fighter facing right: 5 neutral), pressed: the actions pressed then, directions aside }], one entry each time the direction changes or a button is pressed: an input display draws it; sequence() and motion() read it (section 10h: a kit without it has none)\n- `input.hold(a, on = true)`: hold an action down (on) or let it go (false), as its key would\n- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n- `input.longPress()` †: [x, y] the step a press held still has been held .45 s (a long press), else null\n- `input.motion(digits, button, o = {})` †: a fighter's move in numpad notation, mirrored by facing: input.motion('236', 'attack', { facing: hero.facing, window }) is a quarter circle forward and punch (down, down-forward, forward, attack: a fireball); '623' a dragon punch, '41236' a half circle. facing: 1 (right, the default) or -1. button: an action, 'attack+kick', or none (the motion alone)\n- `input.mouseScreen()`: mouse position in projected screen pixels, or null\n- `input.move()`: movement intent in screen directions: x right, y down, length <= 1\n- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n- `input.pan()` †: [dx, dy] how far a drag moved this step: one finger on open ground (not a box), or a mouse's middle or right button; else null. A free camera pans by it (game.cam.free)\n- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n- `input.press(code)`: press a key or button code ('KeyJ', 'Mouse0', 'Pad0', 'Act:attack') as if the person did: scripted input, tests, bots\n- `input.pressed(a)`: true only during the first update step after the press (menus, jumps, one-shot actions)\n- `input.rebind(a, device, code)` †: bind action a to one code for a device ('keys' = keyboard and mouse, 'pad' = gamepad), in place of that device's codes: input.rebind('attack', 'keys', 'KeyF'). Returns null when done, the action that already uses the code (nothing changes: free it first), or 'reserved' for the codes the menus keep (Escape, Enter, F keys, Start, the d-pad). The arrow keys and the d-pad always move as well\n- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: { a: false } } })\n- `input.release(code)`: let go of a code pressed with press()\n- `input.released(a)`: true only during the first update step after the action was let go\n- `input.repeat(a, delay = .3, rate = .08)`: pressed, then repeats while held (after `delay` s, every `rate` s): menu cursors, puzzle pieces\n- `input.resetBindings()` †: forget the player's bindings: every action back to its preset's codes\n- `input.rumble(strength = .5, seconds = .15)` †: shake the gamepad: strength 0..1 for seconds (scaled by rumbleScale; nothing where the controller can't). Returns true when it rumbled\n- `input.screenPoint(cx, cy)` †: browser client coords -> screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space, with no camera), or null without a canvas\n- `input.sequence(steps, o = {})` †: true on the step a sequence of inputs ends, each one after the last within window seconds (.5) of the first: input.sequence(['down', 'down+right', 'right', 'attack']). A step names actions joined by +: its directions are held exactly as it says (up, down, left, right; 'neutral' for none) as they change to that, its buttons pressed. A cheat code: input.sequence(['up', 'up', 'down', 'down', 'left', 'right', 'left', 'right', 'kick', 'attack'], { window: 3 })\n- `input.stopRumble()` †: stop a rumble now (pause, focus lost, unplugged)\n- `input.suppress(a)` †: Suppress a held action until the next tick (a HUD widget owns the pointer this step).\n## 2. Pixel primitives\n\n- `E.px`: the pixel primitives: px.rect, px.line, px.dot, px.disc, px.poly, px.sprite, ... (each snaps to whole pixels)\n- `px.blend(g, a, mode, fn)`: draw fn() at alpha a (stepped, like PS1 hardware) with a blend mode: 'normal', 'add', 'multiply', 'screen' (E.style.trans = 'dither' dithers instead)\n- `px.col(g, c)`: set the fill color (px.* do it themselves)\n- `px.ddisc(g, cx, cy, r, c, a, wx = 0, wy = 0)`: soft disc that fades toward its edge (glows, smoke, dust): stepped alpha rings, or dithering in 'dither' style\n- `px.disc(g, cx, cy, r, c)`: a filled circle\n- `px.dot(g, x, y, c)`: one pixel\n- `px.ell(g, cx, cy, rx, ry, c)`: a filled ellipse\n- `px.glow(g, e = 1)`: GPU lighting: what follows glows (0..1). No effect in Canvas mode, so call it freely.\n- `px.line(g, x0, y0, x1, y1, c, w = 1)`: a line w pixels thick, no smoothing\n- `px.poly(g, pts, c)`: a filled polygon through [[x, y], ...]\n- `px.polyDither(g, pts, c, a, wx = 0, wy = 0)`: translucent polygon: a = 0..1 opacity (stepped alpha, or a dither pattern in 'dither' style). wx/wy = world pixel offset for the pattern\n- `px.rect(g, x, y, w, h, c)`: a filled rectangle, snapped to whole pixels\n- `px.reset(g)`: forget the color cache (after drawing on g with the canvas API directly)\n- `px.sprite(g, spr, x, y, flip = false)`: draw a sprite with its top-left corner at buffer pixel (x, y). flip mirrors it left-right; or o: { flip, rot (radians, turned about its center: E.rotSprite), steps, scale (nearest-neighbour) }\n- `E.sprite(rows, colors = {}, scale = 1)`: Pixel sprite written as strings. Each character is one pixel; colors maps a character to a hex color; '.' and ' ' are transparent. scale (whole number) enlarges each pixel. const COIN = E.sprite(['.yy.', 'yYYy', 'yYYy', '.yy.'], { y: '#f0b020', Y: '#fff0a0' }); Draw it with r.sprite(x, y, z, COIN) (depth sorted) or px.sprite(g, COIN, sx, sy).\n- `E.style: trans`: Translucency style. 'alpha' (default, PS1 / N64 / SNES color math): real transparency in 1/8 steps, plus blend modes. 'dither' (NES, Game Boy, Genesis look): ordered-dither patterns. Set E.style.trans = 'dither' for the older look.\n\n## 2b. Sprite frames, turns and swaps\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '6307,6420p' vendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js && sed -n '6722,6970p' vendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js\"","aggregated_output":"class PlatformMap {\n  /** { rows: [...ASCII, top row first...], legend: { '#': 1, '@': 'hero' }, types: { 1: {...} }, tile: 16, depth: 16 }.\n   *  Tile kinds: 'solid' (default) | 'oneway' | 'ladder' | 'slope' | 'hazard' | 'deco' | 'back' */\n  constructor(o = {}) {\n    /** T: the tile size (16); depth: how deep tiles are drawn in tilted views, world units (the tile size) */\n    this.T = o.tile || 16; this.depth = o.depth === undefined ? this.T : o.depth;\n    const L = o.rows ? parseLevel(o.rows, o.legend) : o.level;\n    if (!L) throw new Error('PlatformMap needs { rows: [...], legend: {...}, types: {...} }');\n    /** w, h: the level's size in cells; types: the tile types by id, with their defaults filled in ({ kind, style,\n     *  side, top, ... }) */\n    this.w = L.w; this.h = L.h; this.types = {};\n    for (const k in (o.types || {})) { const t = Object.assign({ kind: 'solid' }, o.types[k]); t.style = t.style || PT_STYLE_FOR_KIND[t.kind] || 'block'; t.side = t.side || t.color || (t.mat && (material(t.mat, null, 'tile material') || {}).color) || PT_DEFAULT.side; this.types[k] = t; }\n    // stored bottom row first: cz = 0 is the lowest row and z grows upward\n    this.cells = new Array(this.w * this.h).fill(0);\n    for (let y = 0; y < this.h; y++) for (let x = 0; x < this.w; x++) this.cells[(this.h - 1 - y) * this.w + x] = L.cells[y * this.w + x];\n    for (const id of new Set(this.cells)) if (id > 0 && !this.types[id]) { warn('ptype:' + id, 'PlatformMap: tile type ' + id + ' is used but missing from types (using a plain solid block)'); this.types[id] = Object.assign({}, PT_DEFAULT); }\n    /** spawn points: { tag, ch, cx, cz, x, y: 0, z } with x = cell center and z = bottom of the cell (feet) */\n    this.spawns = L.spawns.map(sp => { const cz = this.h - 1 - sp.cy; return Object.assign(sp, { cz, x: (sp.cx + .5) * this.T, y: 0, z: cz * this.T }); });\n    /** version: counts every change to the cells (set); edges: 'solid' (the default) makes the level's left and\n     *  right edges walls, 'open' lets bodies walk off them */\n    this.version = 0; this._bake = null; this.edges = o.edges || 'solid';\n  }\n  /** the first spawn with this tag ({ x, y: 0, z, cx, cz }), or null */\n  find(tag) { return this.spawns.find(s => s.tag === tag) || null; }\n  /** every spawn with this tag */\n  findAll(tag) { return this.spawns.filter(s => s.tag === tag); }\n  /** tile id at column cx, row cz (cz = 0 is the bottom). Left and right of the level are solid walls unless edges: 'open' */\n  cell(cx, cz) { if (cx < 0 || cx >= this.w) return this.edges === 'open' ? 0 : -1; if (cz < 0 || cz >= this.h) return 0; return this.cells[cz * this.w + cx]; }\n  /** a cell's kind: 'solid', 'oneway', 'ladder', 'slope', 'hazard', 'deco' or 'back', null when empty ('solid'\n   *  outside) */\n  kind(cx, cz) { const c = this.cell(cx, cz); return c < 0 ? 'solid' : c === 0 ? null : this.types[c].kind; }\n  /** put tile type id at a cell (0 clears it; cz counts from the bottom row); bumps version */\n  set(cx, cz, id) {\n    if (cx < 0 || cz < 0 || cx >= this.w || cz >= this.h) return;\n    if (id > 0 && !this.types[id]) this.types[id] = Object.assign({}, PT_DEFAULT);\n    this.cells[cz * this.w + cx] = id; this.version++;\n  }\n  /** a world point -> [cx, cz] */\n  toCell(x, z) { return [Math.floor(x / this.T), Math.floor(z / this.T)]; }\n  /** a cell's center -> [x, z] */\n  center(cx, cz) { return [(cx + .5) * this.T, (cz + .5) * this.T]; }\n  /** kind() at a world point */\n  kindAt(x, z) { return this.kind(Math.floor(x / this.T), Math.floor(z / this.T)); }\n  /** true where a world point is inside a solid tile */\n  solidAt(x, z) { return this.kindAt(x, z) === 'solid'; }\n  /** width and height of the level in world units */\n  get width() { return this.w * this.T; }\n  /** the level's height in world units (width is its width) */\n  get height() { return this.h * this.T; }\n  /** top of the highest solid or one-way tile at or below height z in this column, or null over a pit */\n  groundBelow(x, z) {\n    const T = this.T, cx = Math.floor(x / T);\n    for (let cz = Math.min(this.h - 1, Math.floor((z + .5) / T)); cz >= 0; cz--) {\n      const k = this.kind(cx, cz);\n      if (k === 'slope') { const sz = this.slopeZ(cx, cz, x); if (sz <= z + .5) return sz; }\n      else if ((k === 'solid' || k === 'oneway') && (cz + 1) * T <= z + .5) return (cz + 1) * T;\n    }\n    return null;\n  }\n  /** surface height of a slope tile at world x */\n  slopeZ(cx, cz, x) {\n    const t = this.types[this.cell(cx, cz)] || {}, T = this.T, u = clamp((x - cx * T) / T, 0, 1);\n    const a = t.from !== undefined ? t.from : (t.dir < 0 ? 1 : 0), b = t.to !== undefined ? t.to : (t.dir < 0 ? 0 : 1);\n    return cz * T + lerp(a, b, u) * T;\n  }\n  /** highest surface (tile top or slope) under the body within maxDrop below its feet, or null */\n  _surfaceBelow(b, maxDrop) {\n    const T = this.T, hw = b.w / 2 - .01, sc = Math.floor(b.x / T); let best = null;\n    for (let cz = Math.floor((b.z + .01) / T); cz >= Math.floor((b.z - maxDrop) / T) - 1; cz--) {\n      for (let cx = Math.floor((b.x - hw) / T); cx <= Math.floor((b.x + hw) / T); cx++) {\n        const k = this.kind(cx, cz), top = (cz + 1) * T;\n        let sz = null;\n        if (k === 'slope') { if (cx === sc) sz = this.slopeZ(cx, cz, b.x); }\n        else if (k === 'solid' || ((k === 'oneway') && !(b.drop > 0))) sz = top;\n        if (sz !== null && sz <= b.z + .01 && sz >= b.z - maxDrop && (best === null || sz > best)) best = sz;\n      }\n    }\n    return best;\n  }\n  /** tiles overlapped by a body box { x, z, w, h }: [{ cx, cz, id, kind }] (optionally only one kind or id) */\n  cellsTouching(b, what) {\n    const T = this.T, out = [], x0 = Math.floor((b.x - b.w / 2 + .01) / T), x1 = Math.floor((b.x + b.w / 2 - .01) / T), z0 = Math.floor((b.z + .01) / T), z1 = Math.floor((b.z + b.h - .01) / T);\n    for (let cz = z0; cz <= z1; cz++) for (let cx = x0; cx <= x1; cx++) {\n      const id = this.cell(cx, cz); if (id <= 0) continue; const k = this.types[id].kind;\n      if (what === undefined || what === k || what === id) out.push({ cx, cz, id, kind: k });\n    }\n    return out;\n  }\n  /** does the body box overlap a tile of this kind ('hazard', 'ladder', ...) or id? */\n  touching(b, what) { return this.cellsTouching(b, what).length > 0; }\n  /**\n   * Move a body { x, z, vx, vz, w, h } (x = center, z = feet, vz > 0 = up) by its velocity, colliding with the level.\n   * Sets b.onGround, b.onOneWay, b.hitWall (-1 left, 1 right, 0), b.hitCeiling, b.bumped ({ cx, cz, id } of a ceiling\n   * tile hit from below, for ? blocks and bricks) and b.ground (the moving solid it stands on).\n   * One-way tiles hold the body from above unless b.drop > 0. solids: optional array of extra boxes\n   * { x, z, w, h, vx, vz, oneway } (moving platforms, elevators, crates) that also carry what stands on them.\n   */\n  move(b, dt, solids) {\n    const gr = b.ground, wasGround = !!b.onGround;\n    if (gr && solids && solids.includes(gr)) { b.x += (gr.vx || 0) * dt; b.z += (gr.vz || 0) * dt; }\n    b._grounded = wasGround;\n    b.hitWall = 0; b.hitCeiling = false; b.bumped = null; b.onGround = false; b.onOneWay = false; b.ground = null;\n    let dx = (b.vx || 0) * dt, dz = (b.vz || 0) * dt;\n    const n = Math.max(1, Math.ceil(Math.max(Math.abs(dx), Math.abs(dz)) / (this.T * .4)));\n    dx /= n; dz /= n;\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { if (dx && this._mx(b, dx, solids)) dx = 0; if (this._mz(b, dz, solids) && dz > 0) dz = 0; }\n    if (!b.onGround && (b.vz || 0) <= 0) this._probe(b, solids);\n    // stick to the ground when walking down slopes or small steps (never while jumping or climbing)\n    if (!b.onGround && wasGround && (b.vz || 0) <= 0 && !b.climbing) { const sz = this._surfaceBelow(b, Math.max(b.w / 2 + 3, Math.abs(b.vx || 0) * dt * 1.5 + 2)); if (sz !== null) { b.z = sz; b.vz = 0; b.onGround = true; } }\n    return b;\n  }\n  _stands(k, cx, cz, prevZ, top, b) {\n    if (k === 'solid') return true;\n    if (b.drop > 0 || prevZ < top - .01) return false;\nclass Platformer {\n  constructor(o = {}) {\n    /** x, z: its feet's position (side view: x right, z up); y: its depth (0); vx, vz: its speed; w, h: its box (x is\n     *  its center, z its feet); run: top running speed; accel, decel, airAccel: how fast it speeds up and slows down\n     *  on the ground and in the air; jump: the jump's starting speed; gravity: while rising; fallGravity: while\n     *  falling (snappier landings); maxFall: the fastest fall; cut: the share of upward speed kept when jump is let\n     *  go early (short hops); coyote: seconds a jump still works after walking off a ledge; buffer: seconds a jump\n     *  pressed before landing is kept; climb: ladder speed; airJumps: extra jumps in the air (1 = double jump);\n     *  wallJump: jumps off walls; wallSlide: the slowest fall against a wall; dash: dash speed (0 = no dash);\n     *  dashTime: seconds a dash lasts; facing: 1 right, -1 left; onGround: standing on something; climbing: on a\n     *  ladder; jumped, landed: it jumped or landed this step; air: in the air, not climbing; stun: seconds of\n     *  knockback left (no control); drop: seconds left of dropping through a one-way platform; dashing: seconds of\n     *  dash left */\n    Object.assign(this, {\n      x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, vx: 0, vz: 0, w: 8, h: 22,\n      run: 95, accel: 900, decel: 1100, airAccel: 650, jump: 285, gravity: 800, fallGravity: 1150, maxFall: 330,\n      cut: .45, coyote: .09, buffer: .13, climb: 70, airJumps: 0, wallJump: false, wallSlide: 70, dash: 0, dashTime: .22,\n      facing: 1, onGround: false, climbing: false, jumped: false, landed: false, air: false, stun: 0, drop: 0, dashing: 0\n    }, o);\n    this._coy = 0; this._airJ = 0; this._cut = true; this._dashCD = 0;\n  }\n  /** push the body (getting hit): dir = -1 / 1 */\n  knock(dir, speed = 130, up = 170, stun = .3) { this.vx = dir * speed; this.vz = up; this.stun = stun; this.climbing = false; this.dashing = 0; }\n  /** hang from a point (a grapple's hook, a whip's ring): a pendulum from (x, z) to its hands, len long (the distance\n   *  now by default); left and right pump it, jump lets go with its speed (release() does too) */\n  swingFrom(x, z, len) {\n    const hx = this.x, hz = this.z + this.h, L = len || Math.max(8, Math.hypot(hx - x, hz - z)), a = Math.atan2(hx - x, z - hz);\n    /** swinging: the point it swings from ({ x, z, L: the length, a: the angle, w: the angular speed }), or null */\n    this.swinging = { x, z, L, a, w: (this.vx * Math.cos(a) + this.vz * Math.sin(a)) / L };\n    /** hanging: the ledge it hangs from ({ dir, top, cx }), or null; onBars: the bars it hangs from ({ z }), or null;\n     *  onRope: true while on a rope (section 16c sets them) */\n    this.hanging = this.onBars = this.onRope = null; this.climbing = false; this.dashing = 0;\n    return this;\n  }\n  /** let go of a swing, keeping its speed (up: an extra upward speed) */\n  release(up = 0) {\n    const S = this.swinging; if (!S) return this;\n    this.vx = S.L * S.w * Math.cos(S.a); this.vz = S.L * S.w * Math.sin(S.a) + up; this.swinging = null; this._fling = true;   // (its speed kept until it lands)\n    if (Math.abs(this.vx) > 1) this.facing = this.vx > 0 ? 1 : -1;\n    return this;\n  }\n  /** state for Humanoid.update: rig.update(dt, hero.rigState({ attack })) */\n  rigState(extra) { return Object.assign({ x: this.x, y: this.y, z: this.z, vx: this.vx, vy: 0, vz: this.vz, facing: this.facing > 0 ? 0 : Math.PI, air: this.air && !this.climbing, climb: !!this.climbing, hurt: this.stun > 0, dash: this.dashing > 0 }, this._travRig && this._travRig(), extra); }   // (the further moves' poses: section 16c)\n  /** move it one step: ctl is game.input or an intent { x: -1..1, jump, jumpPressed, up, down, dash } (enemies,\n   *  bots); solids: moving platforms [{ x, z, w, h, vx, vz }] to stand on */\n  update(dt, level, ctl = {}, solids) {\n    let ix, jumpHeld, jumpPressed, up, down, dashPressed, consume = () => {};\n    if (ctl && typeof ctl.move === 'function') {   // an E.Input\n      ix = ctl.move()[0]; jumpHeld = ctl.down('jump'); jumpPressed = ctl.buffered('jump', this.buffer); up = ctl.down('up'); down = ctl.down('down');\n      dashPressed = this.dash > 0 && !!ctl.map.dash && ctl.buffered('dash', .1); consume = a => ctl.consume(a);\n    } else { ix = ctl.x || 0; jumpHeld = !!ctl.jump; jumpPressed = !!ctl.jumpPressed; up = !!ctl.up; down = !!ctl.down; dashPressed = !!ctl.dash; }\n    if (Math.abs(ix) < .25) ix = 0;\n    const wasGround = this.onGround; this.jumped = false; this.landed = false;\n    this.stun -= dt; this.drop -= dt; this._dashCD -= dt;\n    const ok = this.stun <= 0;\n    // the further moves (section 16c: crouch, ledges, clinging, water, ropes, bars, swinging, momentum) may take the step\n    if (this._trav && this._trav(dt, level, { ix, jumpHeld, jumpPressed, up, down, dashPressed, consume }, solids, ok)) { if (this.onGround && !wasGround) this.landed = true; this.air = !this.onGround && !this.climbing; return this; }\n    // ladders: grab with up (or down at the top of one), leave with jump or by climbing off the end\n    const feet = { x: this.x, z: this.z - 3, w: 2, h: 3 }, body = { x: this.x, z: this.z, w: 2, h: this.h * .8 };\n    const ladHere = level.touching(body, 'ladder'), ladBelow = level.touching(feet, 'ladder');\n    if (!this.climbing && ok && ((up && ladHere) || (down && ladBelow && this.onGround))) {\n      const lc = level.cellsTouching(up ? body : feet, 'ladder')[0]; this.climbing = true; this.x = (lc.cx + .5) * level.T; this.vx = 0; this.dashing = 0;\n      if (down) this.z -= 2;\n    }\n    if (this.climbing) {\n      this.vz = (up ? 1 : down ? -1 : 0) * this.climb; this.vx = 0;\n      if (jumpPressed) { consume('jump'); this.climbing = false; if (ix) { this.vz = this.jump * .6; this.vx = ix * this.run; } }\n      level.move(this, dt, solids);\n      if (!level.touching({ x: this.x, z: this.z, w: 2, h: this.h }, 'ladder') || (this.onGround && down)) this.climbing = false;\n    } else {\n      // dash (Mega Man X style)\n      if (dashPressed && ok && this._dashCD <= 0) { consume('dash'); this.dashing = this.dashTime; this._dashCD = this.dashTime + .15; this.vz = Math.max(0, this.vz); }\n      if (this.dashing > 0) { this.dashing -= dt; this.vx = this.facing * this.dash; if (!this.onGround) this.vz = Math.max(this.vz, 0); }\n      else if (!this._hx) {   // (_hx: momentum moved it, _spd: a crouch's crawl, _fr: the ground's grip: section 16c)\n        const target = ok ? ix * this.run * (this._spd || 1) : this.vx, turning = ix && this.vx && Math.sign(ix) !== Math.sign(this.vx);\n        const a = (this.onGround ? (ix ? (turning ? this.decel * 1.3 : this.accel) : this.decel) : this.airAccel) * (this._fr || 1);\n        this.vx = ok ? approach(this.vx, target, a * dt) : approach(this.vx, 0, 300 * dt);\n      }\n      if (ix && ok && this.dashing <= 0) this.facing = ix > 0 ? 1 : -1;\n      if (!(this.dashing > 0 && !this.onGround)) this.vz = Math.max(-this.maxFall, this.vz - (this.vz > 0 ? this.gravity : this.fallGravity) * dt);\n      if (!jumpHeld && this.vz > 0 && !this._cut) { this.vz *= this.cut; this._cut = true; }   // let go early = lower jump\n      if (this.onGround) { this._coy = this.coyote; this._airJ = this.airJumps; } else this._coy -= dt;\n      const wall = this.wallJump && !this.onGround && this.hitWall;\n      if (wall && this.vz < -this.wallSlide) this.vz = -this.wallSlide;\n      if (jumpPressed && ok) {\n        if (down && this.onGround && this.onOneWay) { consume('jump'); this.drop = .25; this.onGround = false; this._coy = 0; this._airJ = 0; }\n        else if (this.onGround || this._coy > 0) { consume('jump'); this.vz = this.jump; this._coy = 0; this.jumped = true; this._cut = false; }\n        else if (wall) { consume('jump'); this.vz = this.jump * .95; this.vx = -this.hitWall * this.run * 1.1; this.facing = -this.hitWall; this.stun = .12; this.jumped = true; this._cut = false; }\n        else if (this._airJ > 0) { consume('jump'); this._airJ--; this.vz = this.jump * .9; this.jumped = true; this._cut = false; }\n      }\n      const pushing = this.hitWall, cv = this._carry || 0; if (cv) this.vx += cv;   // (a conveyor's carry: section 16c)\n      level.move(this, dt, solids); if (cv && this.vx) this.vx -= cv;\n      if (!this.hitWall && pushing && ix === pushing && !this.onGround) this.hitWall = pushing;   // keep wall contact while holding toward it\n    }\n    if (this._travAfter) this._travAfter(dt, level);   // (springs and crumbling blocks underfoot: section 16c)\n    if (this.onGround && !wasGround) this.landed = true;\n    this.air = !this.onGround && !this.climbing;\n    return this;\n  }\n}\nE.Platformer = Platformer;\n\n/* =============================================================================\n * 16c. TRAVERSAL  the Platformer's further moves, each opt-in (today's defaults are unchanged), and the rig's poses for\n *    them. Options: crouch (down crouches into a box half as tall: crawl under a gap), ledge (catch a ledge falling past\n *    it: hang, climb up with up or jump, drop with down), wallCling (hold onto a wall pressed in the air; jump leaps off),\n *    momentum (slopes speed it up downhill and slow it uphill, past its run speed up to top; down while running rolls;\n *    down while still and jump charges a dash, let go of down to go). Tiles: 'water' (it swims: less gravity, drag, a\n *    stroke on each jump, a leap out at the surface), 'rope' (up grabs it: climb hand over hand, jump off sideways),\n *    'bars' (rising into them it hangs and travels under them; down or jump lets go), and on any tile type friction (ice:\n *    .15), carry (a conveyor's speed), bounce (a spring's jump speed), crumble (seconds it holds once stood on, then falls\n *    away until respawn seconds pass: level.update(dt) each step). swingFrom(x, z) hangs it from a point (a grapple, a\n *    whip): a pendulum it pumps with left and right, let go of with jump at its speed. State for the rig and the game:\n *    crouching, hanging, climbUp, clinging, swimming, onRope, onBars, swinging, rolling, charge, sprung, splash.\n * ============================================================================= */\n// the tile underfoot ({ cx, cz, t }: its type), or null\nfunction _underfoot(b, level) {\n  const T = level.T, cz = Math.floor((b.z - .5) / T);\n  for (const x of [b.x, b.x - b.w / 2 + 1, b.x + b.w / 2 - 1]) { const cx = Math.floor(x / T), id = level.cell(cx, cz); if (id > 0) return { cx, cz, t: level.types[id] }; }\n  return null;\n}\n// is any cell a box overlaps solid (the level's edges count)?\nfunction _solidIn(level, b) {\n  const T = level.T;\n  for (let cz = Math.floor((b.z + .01) / T); cz <= Math.floor((b.z + b.h - .01) / T); cz++) for (let cx = Math.floor((b.x - b.w / 2 + .01) / T); cx <= Math.floor((b.x + b.w / 2 - .01) / T); cx++) if (level.kind(cx, cz) === 'solid') return true;\n  return false;\n}\n// the ground's slope under the body's center: rise over run (+ rises to the right), 0 when flat\nfunction _slopeUnder(level, b) {\n  const T = level.T, sc = Math.floor(b.x / T);\n  for (const cz of [Math.floor((b.z - .5) / T), Math.floor((b.z + .5) / T)]) if (level.kind(sc, cz) === 'slope') {\n    const t = level.types[level.cell(sc, cz)] || {}, a = t.from !== undefined ? t.from : (t.dir < 0 ? 1 : 0), c = t.to !== undefined ? t.to : (t.dir < 0 ? 0 : 1);\n    return c - a;\n  }\n  return 0;\n}\nObject.assign(Platformer.prototype, {\n  // the step's further moves: true when one of them took the whole step (c: the read input)\n  _trav(dt, level, c, solids, ok) {\n    this._spd = 1; this._fr = 1; this._carry = 0; this._hx = false; this.sprung = false; this.splash = 0;\n    if (!level.cell || !level.types) return false;   // (a level that is not a PlatformMap)\n    const T = level.T, h0 = this._h0 === undefined ? (this._h0 = this.h) : this._h0, consume = c.consume;\n    this._ledgeCD = (this._ledgeCD || 0) - dt; this._clingCD = (this._clingCD || 0) - dt; this._holdCD = (this._holdCD || 0) - dt;\n    const step = () => { level.move(this, dt, solids); return true; };\n    // a swing: the pendulum's angle and speed, pumped by left and right\n    if (this.swinging) {\n      const S = this.swinging;\n      S.w += (-this.gravity / S.L * Math.sin(S.a) + c.ix * (this.pump || 4) * Math.cos(S.a) * 32 / S.L) * dt; S.w *= 1 - .2 * dt; S.a = clamp(S.a + S.w * dt, -2.4, 2.4);\n      const tx = S.x + S.L * Math.sin(S.a), tz = S.z - S.L * Math.cos(S.a) - this.h;\n      this.vx = (tx - this.x) / dt; this.vz = (tz - this.z) / dt; step();\n      if (this.hitWall || this.hitCeiling || this.onGround) S.w *= -.3;\n      if (c.ix) this.facing = c.ix > 0 ? 1 : -1;\n      if (c.jumpPressed) { consume('jump'); this.release(140); this.jumped = true; this._cut = false; }\n      else { this.vx = S.L * S.w * Math.cos(S.a); this.vz = S.L * S.w * Math.sin(S.a); }\n      return true;\n    }\n    // climbing up onto a ledge: hands pull the body up, then a step onto the top\n    if (this.climbUp) {\n      const C = this.climbUp, u = clamp((C.t += dt) / C.dur, 0, 1), k = clamp(u / .6, 0, 1);\n      this.z = lerp(C.z0, C.z1, k * k * (3 - 2 * k)); this.x = lerp(C.x0, C.x1, clamp((u - .6) / .4, 0, 1)); this.vx = this.vz = 0;\n      if (u >= 1) { this.climbUp = null; this.onGround = true; this.z = C.z1; }\n      return true;\n    }\n    // hanging from a ledge\n    if (this.hanging) {\n      const H = this.hanging; this.vx = this.vz = 0; this.facing = H.dir;\n      if (c.jumpPressed && c.ix === -H.dir) { consume('jump'); this.hanging = null; this._ledgeCD = .3; this.vz = this.jump * .85; this.vx = -H.dir * this.run; this.facing = -H.dir; this.jumped = true; this._cut = false; return step(); }\n      if (c.up || c.jumpPressed) { if (c.jumpPressed) consume('jump'); this.hanging = null; this.climbUp = { t: 0, dur: .4, x0: this.x, z0: this.z, x1: H.dir > 0 ? H.cx * T + this.w / 2 + 2 : (H.cx + 1) * T - this.w / 2 - 2, z1: H.top }; return true; }\n      if (c.down) { this.hanging = null; this._ledgeCD = .35; this.vz = -40; }\n      return true;\n    }\n    // water: it swims while its middle is in a water tile\n    if (level.kindAt(this.x, this.z + this.h * (this.swimming ? .3 : .5)) === 'water') {\n      if (!this.swimming) { this.splash = Math.min(1, Math.abs(this.vz) / 300 + .3); this.vz *= .3; this.vx *= .6; }\n      this.swimming = true; this.climbing = false; this.dashing = 0; this.crouching = false; this.h = h0; this.onRope = this.onBars = null;\n      const sw = this.swimSpeed || this.run * .7, head = level.kindAt(this.x, this.z + this.h + 1) === 'water';\n      this.vx = approach(this.vx, c.ix * sw, 420 * dt);\n      const surf = level.kindAt(this.x, this.z + this.h * .62) !== 'water';   // (its head and shoulders out: floating)\n      this.vz = approach(this.vz, c.down ? -sw * .8 : surf ? (c.up ? 0 : -6) : c.up ? sw * .8 : -18, 320 * dt);   // it sinks slowly; at the surface it floats\n      if (c.jumpPressed) { consume('jump'); if (surf || !head) { this.vz = this.jump * .9; this.jumped = true; this._cut = false; this.splash = .6; } else { this.vz = Math.max(this.vz, 110); this.stroke = .45; } }\n      this.stroke = Math.max(0, (this.stroke || 0) - dt);\n      if (c.ix) this.facing = c.ix > 0 ? 1 : -1;\n      return step();\n    }\n    if (this.swimming) { this.swimming = false; this.splash = .5; }\n    // a rope: up grabs it; climb hand over hand; jump leaves it sideways\n    const ropeBox = { x: this.x, z: this.z, w: 2, h: this.h }, onRope = level.touching(ropeBox, 'rope');\n    if (!onRope) this.onRope = false;\n    if (!this.onRope && onRope && c.up && ok && this._holdCD <= 0) { const rc = level.cellsTouching(ropeBox, 'rope')[0]; this.onRope = true; this.x = (rc.cx + .5) * T; this.dashing = 0; }\n    if (this.onRope) {\n      const top = level.kindAt(this.x, this.z + this.h * .9 + 1) === 'rope';\n      this.vz = (c.up && top ? 1 : c.down ? -1 : 0) * this.climb * .85; this.vx = 0; this.climbing = true;\n      if (c.ix) this.facing = c.ix > 0 ? 1 : -1;\n      if (c.jumpPressed) { consume('jump'); this.onRope = false; this.climbing = false; this._holdCD = .25; this.vz = this.jump * .7; this.vx = (c.ix || this.facing) * this.run; this.jumped = true; this._cut = false; return step(); }\n      step(); if (this.onGround && c.down) { this.onRope = false; this.climbing = false; }\n      return true;\n    }\n    // monkey bars: rising (or falling) into them, the hands catch them; it travels under them\n    const handZ = this.z + this.h + 2;\n    if (!this.onBars && !this.onGround && this._holdCD <= 0 && ok && level.kindAt(this.x, handZ) === 'bars') this.onBars = { z: Math.floor(handZ / T) * T };\n    if (this.onBars) {\n      const bz = this.onBars.z; this.z = bz - this.h; this.vz = 0; this.vx = c.ix * this.run * .55; this.dashing = 0;\n      if (c.ix) this.facing = c.ix > 0 ? 1 : -1;\n      step(); this.z = bz - this.h; this.vz = 0; this.onGround = false;\n      if (c.down || c.jumpPressed || level.kindAt(this.x, bz + 1) !== 'bars') { if (c.jumpPressed) consume('jump'); this.onBars = null; this._holdCD = .3; this.vz = -20; }\n      return true;\n    }\n    // a wall it is pressed against in the air: it clings (no sliding) until it jumps off, lets go or presses down\n    if (this.wallCling && !this.onGround && this.hitWall && c.ix === this.hitWall && this._clingCD <= 0 && ok && this.vz <= 60) this.clinging = this.hitWall;\n    if (this.clinging) {\n      const d = this.clinging; this.vx = this.vz = 0; this.facing = -d;\n      if (c.jumpPressed) { consume('jump'); this.clinging = 0; this._clingCD = .2; this.vz = this.jump * .95; this.vx = -d * this.run * 1.1; this.jumped = true; this._cut = false; this.stun = .12; return step(); }\n      if (c.down || c.ix === -d || !_solidIn(level, { x: this.x + d * (this.w / 2 + 1.5), z: this.z + 2, w: 1, h: this.h - 4 })) { this.clinging = 0; this._clingCD = .25; return false; }\n      step(); this.hitWall = d; return true;\n    }\n    // a ledge falling past it: the hands catch its top\n    if (this.ledge && !this.onGround && this.vz <= 0 && this._ledgeCD <= 0 && ok && !this.climbing) {\n      const d = c.ix || this.facing, cx = Math.floor((this.x + d * (this.w / 2 + 2)) / T), hz = this.z + this.h, cz = Math.floor((hz - 1) / T), top = (cz + 1) * T;\n      if (level.kind(cx, cz) === 'solid' && level.kind(cx, cz + 1) !== 'solid' && level.kind(cx, cz + 2) !== 'solid' && hz >= top - 7 && hz <= top + 3 && !_solidIn(level, { x: this.x, z: top, w: this.w - 1, h: 4 })) {\n        this.hanging = { dir: d, top, cx }; this.x = d > 0 ? cx * T - this.w / 2 - .01 : (cx + 1) * T + this.w / 2 + .01; this.z = top - this.h; this.vx = this.vz = 0; this.facing = d; this.dashing = 0;\n        return true;\n      }\n    }\n    // crouching (and a charged dash with momentum): down on the ground; standing again needs the room\n    const ducks = this.crouch || this.momentum;\n    if (ducks && this.onGround && !this.climbing && ok && !this.rolling && c.down && !this.crouching && !(this.momentum && Math.abs(this.vx) > this.run * .5)) { this.crouching = true; this.h = h0 * .5; }\n    if (this.crouching && (!c.down || !this.onGround) && !_solidIn(level, { x: this.x, z: this.z + h0 * .5, w: this.w - 1, h: h0 * .5 })) {\n      this.crouching = false; this.h = h0;\n      if (this.charge > 0) { this.rolling = true; this.h = h0 * .5; this.vx = this.facing * (this.run * 1.4 + this.charge * this.run * 1.6); this.charge = 0; this.dashed = true; }\n    }\n    if (this.crouching) {\n      if (this.momentum && c.jumpPressed && !(c.down && this.onOneWay)) { consume('jump'); this.charge = Math.min(1, (this.charge || 0) + .3); }\n      else if (c.jumpPressed && this.onOneWay) { consume('jump'); this.drop = .25; this.onGround = false; this.crouching = false; this.h = h0; }\n      if (this.charge > 0) this.charge = Math.max(0, this.charge - dt * .4);\n      this.vx = this.momentum && this.charge > 0 ? 0 : approach(this.vx, c.ix * this.run * (this.crawlSpeed || .45), this.accel * dt);\n      if (c.ix) this.facing = c.ix > 0 ? 1 : -1;\n      this.vz = Math.max(-this.maxFall, this.vz - this.fallGravity * dt);\n      return step();\n    }\n    // the ground's grip underfoot (ice, conveyors)\n    const u = this.onGround ? _underfoot(this, level) : null;\n    if (u) { this._fr = u.t.friction || 1; this._carry = u.t.carry || 0; }\n    // momentum: slopes push it, it keeps speed past its run, a roll keeps going\n    if (this.momentum && ok && !this.climbing) {\n      const top = this.top || this.run * 2.2;\n      if (this.onGround) {\n        const s = _slopeUnder(level, this);\n        let vx = this.vx - s / Math.sqrt(1 + s * s) * this.gravity * (this.rolling ? .9 : .5) * dt;\n        if (this.rolling) vx = approach(vx, 0, 50 * dt);\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
