(th.font && /\\d|\\b(bold|italic|normal|oblique)\\b/.test(th.font)) warn('shell:font', 'E.Shell theme.font is a family (\"Georgia, serif\"), not a CSS shorthand (\"' + th.font + '\"): the size comes f [... omitted end of long line]\n11709:    const scale = Math.max(.5, 1 - foe.combo * .1), dmg = Math.round(m.dmg * scale);\n13400:  place(z, offset, what, scale = 8) {\n  Mouse0: 'Left click', Mouse1: 'Middle click', Mouse2: 'Right click', Mouse3: 'Mouse 4', Mouse4: 'Mouse 5', Backquote: '`', Minus: '-', Equal: '=', BracketLeft: '[',\n  BracketRight: ']', Backslash: '\\\\', Semicolon: ';', Quote: \"'\", Comma: ',', Period: '.', Slash: '/',\n  PadAxisUp: 'L stick ↑', PadAxisDown: 'L stick ↓', PadAxisLeft: 'L stick ←', PadAxisRight: 'L stick →',\n  PadRAxisUp: 'R stick ↑', PadRAxisDown: 'R stick ↓', PadRAxisLeft: 'R stick ←', PadRAxisRight: 'R stick →', WheelUp: 'Wheel up', WheelDown: 'Wheel down' };\n/** top-down / isometric action (Zelda, Diablo): Space dashes, J or click attacks */\nInput.DEFAULT = {\n  up: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp', 'Pad12'], down: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown', 'Pad13'], left: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft', 'Pad14'], right: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight', 'Pad15'],\n  attack: ['KeyJ', 'KeyX', 'Mouse0', 'Pad0', 'Pad7'], dash: ['Space', 'ShiftLeft', 'ShiftRight', 'KeyK', 'Pad1', 'Pad6'],\n  skill: ['KeyL', 'KeyE', 'Mouse2', 'Pad2', 'Pad5'], jump: ['KeyZ', 'Pad3'], ...MENU_KEYS\n};\n/** side-scrollers (Mario, Mega Man): Space / Z / K jump, X / J attack or shoot, Shift / C dash */\nInput.PLATFORMER = {\n  up: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp', 'Pad12'], down: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown', 'Pad13'], left: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft', 'Pad14'], right: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight', 'Pad15'],\n  jump: ['Space', 'KeyZ', 'KeyK', 'Pad0'], attack: ['KeyX', 'KeyJ', 'Mouse0', 'Pad2'], dash: ['ShiftLeft', 'ShiftRight', 'KeyC', 'KeyL', 'Pad1', 'Pad5'],\n  skill: ['KeyE', 'KeyV', 'Mouse2', 'Pad3'], ...MENU_KEYS\n};\n/** third-person action and stealth (Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear): WASD / stick move, Shift sprint, Space jump and parkour,\n *  C crouch (a toggle), E interact, J attack, K block, L dodge, Q use, M map. Pad: A jump, B crouch, X attack, Y interact,\n *  LB block, RB dodge, LT use, RT or L3 sprint, Back map */\nInput.THIRDPERSON = {\n  up: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp', 'Pad12'], down: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown', 'Pad13'], left: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft', 'Pad14'], right: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight', 'Pad15'],\n  sprint: ['ShiftLeft', 'ShiftRight', 'Pad7', 'Pad10'], jump: ['Space', 'Pad0'], crouch: ['KeyC', 'ControlLeft', 'Pad1'], interact: ['KeyE', 'KeyF', 'Pad3'],\n  attack: ['KeyJ', 'Mouse0', 'Pad2'], block: ['KeyK', 'Mouse2', 'Pad4'], dodge: ['KeyL', 'Pad5'], use: ['KeyQ', 'Pad6'], map: ['KeyM', 'Tab', 'Pad8'], ...MENU_KEYS\n};\n/** shoot-'em-ups (1942, Gradius): Space / Z / J fire (hold for autofire), X / K bomb */\nInput.SHMUP = {\n  up: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp', 'Pad12'], down: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown', 'Pad13'], left: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft', 'Pad14'], right: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight', 'Pad15'],\n  fire: ['Space', 'KeyZ', 'KeyJ', 'Mouse0', 'Pad0', 'Pad7'], bomb: ['KeyX', 'KeyK', 'Mouse2', 'Pad1', 'Pad6'], ...MENU_KEYS\n};\nE.Input = Input;\n\n/* =============================================================================\n * 6. PIXEL FONTS  the 5x7 text font (the default) and the 3x5 one for in-world numbers and labels\n * ============================================================================= */\n// Both fonts are tables of glyphs: each entry a character, then one digit for each row of its pixels, top to bottom, the\nfunction _pClaim(game) {   // player 1 reads no pad another player holds; the keyboard's codes go to the players sharing it\n  const P = game.players, I = P[0];\n  I._claimed = new Set(P.slice(1).filter(q => typeof q.pad === 'number').map(q => q.pad));\n  I.keysTo = P.slice(1).filter(q => q.half).concat(game._lobby ? [game._lobby] : []);\n  if (!I.keysTo.length) I.keysTo = null;\n}\n/** let players join, up to max (2..4): Start on a gamepad no one holds, or 2 on the keyboard (o.keys: false not); onJoin\n *  (input, number) as each does. allowJoin(false) closes it (the names split and join are String's and Array's) */\nGame.prototype.allowJoin = function (o = {}) {\n  if (o === false) { this._join = null; this._lobby = null; _pClaim(this); return this; }\n  this._join = { max: clamp(o.max || 2, 2, 4), onJoin: o.onJoin || null, keys: o.keys !== false };\n  this._lobby = this._join.keys && this.screen.canvas ? new Input(_pStub(this), { join: ['Digit2'] }) : null;   // (listens for 2 while player 1 has the whole keyboard)\n  _pClaim(this); return this;\n};\n/** a player in now: { pad: index } (a gamepad) or { keys: 'right' } (the keyboard's right half; player 1 takes the\n *  left). Returns its input (null when four play already) */\nGame.prototype.addPlayer = function (o = {}) {\n  const P = this.players; if (P.length >= 4) return null;\n  const q = new Input(_pStub(this), Input.DEFAULT), n = P.length + 1;\n  Object.assign(q, { player: n, name: 'P' + n, color: E.PLAYER_COLORS[n - 1], pad: typeof o.pad === 'number' ? o.pad : null, half: o.keys ? 'right' : null, device: o.keys ? 'keyboard' : 'gamepad' });\n  for (const k of ['glyphs', 'deadzone', 'invertAimY', 'invertMoveX', 'invertMoveY', 'rumbleScale']) q[k] = this.input[k];   // (the player's settings: button symbols, dead zone, aim, the move stick, vibration)\n  q.lastDevice = q.device; if (q.pad !== null) { q.tick(0); q.consumeAll(); }   // (the buttons held as it joins, its Start among them, are no presses)\n  const I = P[0]; if (q.half && !I.half) { I._full = I.preset; I.half = 'left'; I.use(Input.halfKeys(I._full, 'left')); }   // player 1 moves to the left half\n  q.use(_pPreset(this, q));\n  if (!this.settings.spec('playerBindings')) this.settings.define({ key: 'playerBindings', group: 'Controls', type: 'bindings', value: () => ({}), apply: (g, v) => { for (const p of g.players.slice(1)) p.bindings = (v || {})[p.player] || {}; } });\n  q.bindings = (this.settings.playerBindings || {})[n] || {};\n  q._onBindings = b => this.settings.set('playerBindings', Object.assign({}, this.settings.playerBindings, { [n]: b }));\n  P.push(q); _pClaim(this);\n  if (this._join && this._join.onJoin) try { this._join.onJoin(q, n); } catch (e) { this.fail('allowJoin onJoin', e); }\n  this.note(q.name + ' JOINED', 1.5); this.audio.sfx('confirm');\n  return q;\n};\n/** a player leaves (its input, or its number, 2 to 4); player 1 has the whole keyboard back when no one shares it */\nGame.prototype.removePlayer = function (p) {\n  const P = this.players, i = typeof p === 'number' ? p - 1 : P.indexOf(p); if (i < 1 || i >= P.length) return;\n  P.splice(i, 1); P.forEach((q, k) => { q.player = k + 1; q.name = 'P' + (k + 1); q.color = E.PLAYER_COLORS[k]; });\n  const I = P[0]; if (I.half && !P.some(q => q !== I && q.half)) { I.half = null; I.use(I._full || I.preset); I._full = null; }\n  _pClaim(this);\n};\n/** split the screen into n viewports (2 to 4; 0 or 1: one screen again), o: { layout: 'auto' (side by side on a wide\n *  screen, stacked on a tall one; a grid for 3 or 4) | 'columns' | 'rows' | 'grid', follow: [targets], z: 16, gap: 1 } */\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
