{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_116","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('src/view/mine-view.js');s=p.read_text();s=s.replace('m.chamber === 2','m.room.def.extraction');p.write_text(s)\np=Path('src/main.js');s=p.read_text();s=s.replace(\\\"if (m.chamber === 2) objective\\\", \\\"if (m.room.def.extraction) objective\\\");s=s.replace('(m.chamber < 2 || m.finale.cleared === 3)', '(\"'!m.room.def.extraction || m.finale.cleared === P.EXTRACTION.length)'\"');p.write_text(s)\np=Path('docs/authoring.md');s=p.read_text();s=s.replace(\\\"To add a chamber, add a ROOM record, adjust the expedition's final index/completion condition, and add a matching practice entry (the UI enumerates room records).\\\", \\\"To add a chamber, add a ROOM record; the expedition length and practice entries follow the room catalogue. Mark its extraction flag only when it should use the existing machine-wave setpiece.\\\");s=s.replace('The authoritative \"'`Mine.director` and `updateWarnings` are the encounter authoring points.'\"', '\"'`PD.PATTERNS` and `PD.EXTRACTION` in the content catalogue are the encounter authoring points. A room references a pattern ID containing its door pool, families, optional introductory stages, pair interval, spawn scale and route bias. Copy a record, change its data, and reference that ID from a room to add a new boulder pattern without editing the simulation. `PD.EXTRACTION` declares each wave’s work threshold, collision tier, participating doors and announcement. The core director interprets this data.'\"');p.write_text(s)\nPY\nnode --check src/main.js && node --check src/view/mine-view.js\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
