{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_136","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"node --input-type=module <<'JS'\nimport fs from 'node:fs';\nconst rows = [\n ['Original ore gold seam was occluded by stone geometry',false,'Native asset raster inspection'],\n ['Flywheel spokes were offset from their hub',false,'Native asset raster inspection'],\n ['Route string overwrote numeric door identity and crashed warning emission',true,'Normal native expedition exception'],\n ['Crouch swallowed down at a ladder top, blocking native descent',true,'Native route playthrough and isolated descent regression'],\n ['Expiring ladder grace could reattach forever instead of dismounting',true,'Native route trace and expiry-grace regression'],\n ['Checkpoint retry incorrectly charged the doorway partner-haul fee',false,'Checkpoint score regression in simulation suite'],\n ['Join accepted duplicate seat IDs and aliased ownership',false,'Duplicate-seat simulation regression'],\n ['Timed held poses stayed active after their timer expired',false,'Integration/animation review; native browser playthrough'],\n ['Precreated couch roster caused native second-player input to be rejected',true,'Integration review; browser two-pad independent-control regression'],\n ['Starting solo practice could retain old split-keyboard controls',false,'Integration review; native ownership/browser regression'],\n ['Touch waking attract could click through into a new title option',false,'Actual portrait and landscape touch regression'],\n ['Contextual touch released between ticks lost its action edge',true,'Actual short-touch door regression in both orientations'],\n ['Assisted chop consumed the deliberate touch Redirect opportunity',true,'Actual contextual redirect contact/wear regression'],\n ['Remote local traversal waited for round-trip snapshots',false,'Long hidden-authority playthrough; immediate owner-prediction regression'],\n ['Between-slot jump direction, redirect aim or attack facing could be lost',true,'Per-edge directional context network regressions and six full online routes'],\n ['Closing a results panel could leave a static world without replay choices',false,'Integration flow review; results/replay browser regression'],\n ['A knocked-out midair marker could remain above a reachable rescue landing',false,'Integration review; native gravity now settles downed bodies'],\n ['First-touch hint overlapped the contextual action bubble',false,'Phone screenshot/bounds inspection; both orientations now separated'],\n ['Initial movement hint could name keyboard controls for a pad player',false,'Input/presentation review; native last-device prompt adapter']\n];\nconst issues=rows.map(([description,critical,evidence],i)=>({id:'PD-'+String(i+1).padStart(2,'0'),description,critical,product:true,fixed:true,evidence}));\nfs.writeFileSync('docs/issues.json',JSON.stringify(issues,null,2)+'\\\\n');\nconst f=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('docs/feedback.json','utf8'));\nf.testingFeedback[0]='19 unique issues caught by automated checks, visual checks and integration review; all fixed. The ledger separates review findings from reproduced test failures.';\nf.testingFeedback[1]='7 critical issues affected launch, required controls, progression or simultaneous local co-op; all fixed.';\nf.testingFeedback[2]='Long hidden-authority shared-world playthroughs exposed delayed feedback and lost press direction that short protocol checks missed.';\nf.testingFeedback[3]='Syntax-only checks were least helpful for gameplay: they cannot establish traversal, recovery, co-op ownership or completion.';\nf.engineFeedback[5]='Expose a compact serializable Platformer traversal state with a tested prediction/reconciliation example.';\nfs.writeFileSync('docs/feedback.json',JSON.stringify(f,null,2)+'\\\\n');\nJS\ncat > docs/testing.md <<'EOF'\n# Release verification\n\nFrom the development folder, run **\"'`node tools/verify.mjs`** (also `npm test`). Success prints only one count line. Failures print their case/context and that count. The runner rebuilds the exact root HTML, checks provenance/schema/embedded-script syntax, then runs native simulation, fake-Hub protocol/gameplay, file-browser input/audio and the unchanged official Hub harness. It captures successful child output. All browsers and the OS-selected loopback server are owned by these scripts and closed in `finally`; no shared ports or unrelated processes are touched.\n\nThe final result and SHA-256 of the tested artifact are written to `docs/evidence/verification.json`. `index.html` is generated byte-for-byte from the same bundle as the root deliverable. Feedback comes from one data model, `docs/feedback.json`, embedded into About and written to the root exit-interview.json.\n\n## Coverage\n\n- **67 native simulation/content checks:** row conversion; traversal, variable jumping, coyote/buffer, ducking and permanent/temporary ladder routes; action deduplication, arcs, heavy ore, wear and contact order; damage/invulnerability; seeded supply bounds, expiry/recovery and several unarmed minutes; sole team key and carrier departure; checkpoints/retry/once-only score; rescue/join/camping/wipe; full native snapshots and subsequent RNG/events; validated tuning; 15 solo seed/route expeditions and three simultaneous couch expeditions. See `testing-sim.md` and `pilot-evidence.md`.\n- **29 network checks:** sender/epoch/sequence authentication, repeated edges/acknowledgements, silence neutralization, atomic native views, overtaken keyframes, reliable event deduplication, 10-message combined rate and byte limits, departure/finish/end, hidden authority, owner-only movement prediction and its authority boundary, retained press direction/aim/facing. Six complete canonical expeditions cover all three routes with player-host or hidden authority at 150ms one-way latency, 50ms jitter and 5% unreliable loss. See `network.md`.\n- **40 browser input/audio checks:** final file:// launch; actual keyboard/mouse; injected standard pads and pad-only screens; binding storage, glyphs, ownership/disconnect; co-op start/independent P2/drop-out; a normal-input full browser expedition/results/replay; exact attract boundary/feature loop/wake/reset/records; real CDP multitouch in 390×844 and 844×390; contextual tap/hold/redirect; independent offline audio buses, bounded amplitude, mute/voice-off and live cleanup; WebKit phone launch/touch. See `testing-browser-input.md`.\n- **Official Hub conformance:** unchanged harness.html + bridge.js + round.js at our own origin; one/two seats, 150/50/5 network faults, host leave and hidden nonplayer authority. Both `__hubCheck.pass === true` and body.dataset.complete === '\"'true' are required. Additional assertions check actual game identity/state, countdown/authority, byte/rate bounds and no post-end ticks/traffic. The full hidden-authority + two-client browser expedition uses ordinary production Pilot controls under the same network faults, and asserts keys/doors/tool lifecycle/finale/victory plus the real deadline margin. No catalogue recording options are used.\n\n## Defects\n\n\"'`issues.json` records **19 unique fixed product issues**, including **7 critical** issues. Critical means an issue prevented launch, a required control/progression path or a mandatory mode, or lost authoritative ownership/state. Counts include automated tests, native raster/phone inspections and explicitly labelled integration review findings. Test-author mistakes (locator naming, glyph cycle assumptions, partial-touch event semantics and an accidentally disabled test spawn director) are excluded. Repeated failing assertions for one root cause count once.\n\nThe longer online run was useful precisely because the official short harness already passed: actual client traversal needed prompt owner prediction, and action-edge direction needed reliable context. A separate reactive-Pilot limitation was also corrected using visible warnings and ordinary controls; that controller limitation is not counted as a new product defect. No god mode, teleports, health/resource grants or completion switches are used in full expedition evidence.\n\n## Visual and environmental limits\n\nScreenshots inspect TV typography/composition, miner/ore separation, tool/supply cues, temporary ladders, touch occlusion and native menu focus. Finite CSS animations are completed for static captures. Native assets/animation preview sheets are in docs/. Screenshots supplement state assertions and do not prove a completed mechanic or network round.\n\nPhysical DualSense feel, actual iOS Safari, a real television at viewing distance, public-internet peers and listening quality remain unconfirmed. WebKit, injected pads, same-machine delayed transport and measured audio samples are the available stand-ins. A first-time human 10–12-minute completion target remains unmeasured; skilled scripted runs finish faster without time gates. The Hub deadline stays on its wall clock even in menus or a slow/developer simulation.\nEOF\ncat > README.md <<'\"'EOF'\n# Pick Axe Deplete\n\nBig swing. Small warranty.\n\nAn original three-chamber arcade platformer inspired by Pick Axe Pete (1982). Chop gold-bearing ore, redirect rocks into rich crashes, chase descending tools and rising keys, then prime the extraction machinery. Play solo, simultaneous local co-op, or shared-world co-op inside AI Hub.\n\nOpen the delivered root HTML directly in a browser; it needs no server, install, CDN or asset download. A copy is generated here as \"'`index.html`. AI Hub sessions use its supplied transport and lifecycle; standalone local co-op needs no online service.\n\nMove with A/D or arrows; W/S climbs or ducks. Space jumps, J/left-click chops, Q/right-click redirects, E deliberately enters a door or holds to rescue, Escape pauses. Standard gamepad: stick/D-pad, Cross jump, Square chop, R2 redirect, Circle/down duck, Triangle interact, Options pause. The native Controls screen supports rebinding. Touch: invisible left thumb movement/climb/down, right tap/hold jump, assisted chopping and a contextual action bubble.\n\nThe pause menu includes paged settings, help, About/feedback, Developer tools and standalone checkpoint/replay actions. Developer/practice/attract shifts cannot overwrite completed expedition records. Idle title menus start a real demonstration after ten seconds; waking input is consumed.\n\nBuild: `node tools/build.mjs`.\n\nVerify: `node tools/verify.mjs` (or `npm test`). This is a quiet aggregate with full gameplay/browser/Hub proof and may take several minutes. Uses the already-installed Python Playwright environment described in TASK.md; no browser installation is needed.\n\nAuthoring: `docs/authoring.md`. Research/provenance: `docs/research.md`, `docs/dependencies.md`. Verification and issue ledger: `docs/testing.md`, `docs/issues.json`. Network prediction/authority: `docs/network.md`. Original coded audio and native assets: `docs/audio.md`, `docs/assets.md`.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_136","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"node --input-type=module <<'JS'\nimport fs from 'node:fs';\nconst rows = [\n ['Original ore gold seam was occluded by stone geometry',false,'Native asset raster inspection'],\n ['Flywheel spokes were offset from their hub',false,'Native asset raster inspection'],\n ['Route string overwrote numeric door identity and crashed warning emission',true,'Normal native expedition exception'],\n ['Crouch swallowed down at a ladder top, blocking native descent',true,'Native route playthrough and isolated descent regression'],\n ['Expiring ladder grace could reattach forever instead of dismounting',true,'Native route trace and expiry-grace regression'],\n ['Checkpoint retry incorrectly charged the doorway partner-haul fee',false,'Checkpoint score regression in simulation suite'],\n ['Join accepted duplicate seat IDs and aliased ownership',false,'Duplicate-seat simulation regression'],\n ['Timed held poses stayed active after their timer expired',false,'Integration/animation review; native browser playthrough'],\n ['Precreated couch roster caused native second-player input to be rejected',true,'Integration review; browser two-pad independent-control regression'],\n ['Starting solo practice could retain old split-keyboard controls',false,'Integration review; native ownership/browser regression'],\n ['Touch waking attract could click through into a new title option',false,'Actual portrait and landscape touch regression'],\n ['Contextual touch released between ticks lost its action edge',true,'Actual short-touch door regression in both orientations'],\n ['Assisted chop consumed the deliberate touch Redirect opportunity',true,'Actual contextual redirect contact/wear regression'],\n ['Remote local traversal waited for round-trip snapshots',false,'Long hidden-authority playthrough; immediate owner-prediction regression'],\n ['Between-slot jump direction, redirect aim or attack facing could be lost',true,'Per-edge directional context network regressions and six full online routes'],\n ['Closing a results panel could leave a static world without replay choices',false,'Integration flow review; results/replay browser regression'],\n ['A knocked-out midair marker could remain above a reachable rescue landing',false,'Integration review; native gravity now settles downed bodies'],\n ['First-touch hint overlapped the contextual action bubble',false,'Phone screenshot/bounds inspection; both orientations now separated'],\n ['Initial movement hint could name keyboard controls for a pad player',false,'Input/presentation review; native last-device prompt adapter']\n];\nconst issues=rows.map(([description,critical,evidence],i)=>({id:'PD-'+String(i+1).padStart(2,'0'),description,critical,product:true,fixed:true,evidence}));\nfs.writeFileSync('docs/issues.json',JSON.stringify(issues,null,2)+'\\\\n');\nconst f=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('docs/feedback.json','utf8'));\nf.testingFeedback[0]='19 unique issues caught by automated checks, visual checks and integration review; all fixed. The ledger separates review findings from reproduced test failures.';\nf.testingFeedback[1]='7 critical issues affected launch, required controls, progression or simultaneous local co-op; all fixed.';\nf.testingFeedback[2]='Long hidden-authority shared-world playthroughs exposed delayed feedback and lost press direction that short protocol checks missed.';\nf.testingFeedback[3]='Syntax-only checks were least helpful for gameplay: they cannot establish traversal, recovery, co-op ownership or completion.';\nf.engineFeedback[5]='Expose a compact serializable Platformer traversal state with a tested prediction/reconciliation example.';\nfs.writeFileSync('docs/feedback.json',JSON.stringify(f,null,2)+'\\\\n');\nJS\ncat > docs/testing.md <<'EOF'\n# Release verification\n\nFrom the development folder, run **\"'`node tools/verify.mjs`** (also `npm test`). Success prints only one count line. Failures print their case/context and that count. The runner rebuilds the exact root HTML, checks provenance/schema/embedded-script syntax, then runs native simulation, fake-Hub protocol/gameplay, file-browser input/audio and the unchanged official Hub harness. It captures successful child output. All browsers and the OS-selected loopback server are owned by these scripts and closed in `finally`; no shared ports or unrelated processes are touched.\n\nThe final result and SHA-256 of the tested artifact are written to `docs/evidence/verification.json`. `index.html` is generated byte-for-byte from the same bundle as the root deliverable. Feedback comes from one data model, `docs/feedback.json`, embedded into About and written to the root exit-interview.json.\n\n## Coverage\n\n- **67 native simulation/content checks:** row conversion; traversal, variable jumping, coyote/buffer, ducking and permanent/temporary ladder routes; action deduplication, arcs, heavy ore, wear and contact order; damage/invulnerability; seeded supply bounds, expiry/recovery and several unarmed minutes; sole team key and carrier departure; checkpoints/retry/once-only score; rescue/join/camping/wipe; full native snapshots and subsequent RNG/events; validated tuning; 15 solo seed/route expeditions and three simultaneous couch expeditions. See `testing-sim.md` and `pilot-evidence.md`.\n- **29 network checks:** sender/epoch/sequence authentication, repeated edges/acknowledgements, silence neutralization, atomic native views, overtaken keyframes, reliable event deduplication, 10-message combined rate and byte limits, departure/finish/end, hidden authority, owner-only movement prediction and its authority boundary, retained press direction/aim/facing. Six complete canonical expeditions cover all three routes with player-host or hidden authority at 150ms one-way latency, 50ms jitter and 5% unreliable loss. See `network.md`.\n- **40 browser input/audio checks:** final file:// launch; actual keyboard/mouse; injected standard pads and pad-only screens; binding storage, glyphs, ownership/disconnect; co-op start/independent P2/drop-out; a normal-input full browser expedition/results/replay; exact attract boundary/feature loop/wake/reset/records; real CDP multitouch in 390×844 and 844×390; contextual tap/hold/redirect; independent offline audio buses, bounded amplitude, mute/voice-off and live cleanup; WebKit phone launch/touch. See `testing-browser-input.md`.\n- **Official Hub conformance:** unchanged harness.html + bridge.js + round.js at our own origin; one/two seats, 150/50/5 network faults, host leave and hidden nonplayer authority. Both `__hubCheck.pass === true` and body.dataset.complete === '\"'true' are required. Additional assertions check actual game identity/state, countdown/authority, byte/rate bounds and no post-end ticks/traffic. The full hidden-authority + two-client browser expedition uses ordinary production Pilot controls under the same network faults, and asserts keys/doors/tool lifecycle/finale/victory plus the real deadline margin. No catalogue recording options are used.\n\n## Defects\n\n\"'`issues.json` records **19 unique fixed product issues**, including **7 critical** issues. Critical means an issue prevented launch, a required control/progression path or a mandatory mode, or lost authoritative ownership/state. Counts include automated tests, native raster/phone inspections and explicitly labelled integration review findings. Test-author mistakes (locator naming, glyph cycle assumptions, partial-touch event semantics and an accidentally disabled test spawn director) are excluded. Repeated failing assertions for one root cause count once.\n\nThe longer online run was useful precisely because the official short harness already passed: actual client traversal needed prompt owner prediction, and action-edge direction needed reliable context. A separate reactive-Pilot limitation was also corrected using visible warnings and ordinary controls; that controller limitation is not counted as a new product defect. No god mode, teleports, health/resource grants or completion switches are used in full expedition evidence.\n\n## Visual and environmental limits\n\nScreenshots inspect TV typography/composition, miner/ore separation, tool/supply cues, temporary ladders, touch occlusion and native menu focus. Finite CSS animations are completed for static captures. Native assets/animation preview sheets are in docs/. Screenshots supplement state assertions and do not prove a completed mechanic or network round.\n\nPhysical DualSense feel, actual iOS Safari, a real television at viewing distance, public-internet peers and listening quality remain unconfirmed. WebKit, injected pads, same-machine delayed transport and measured audio samples are the available stand-ins. A first-time human 10–12-minute completion target remains unmeasured; skilled scripted runs finish faster without time gates. The Hub deadline stays on its wall clock even in menus or a slow/developer simulation.\nEOF\ncat > README.md <<'\"'EOF'\n# Pick Axe Deplete\n\nBig swing. Small warranty.\n\nAn original three-chamber arcade platformer inspired by Pick Axe Pete (1982). Chop gold-bearing ore, redirect rocks into rich crashes, chase descending tools and rising keys, then prime the extraction machinery. Play solo, simultaneous local co-op, or shared-world co-op inside AI Hub.\n\nOpen the delivered root HTML directly in a browser; it needs no server, install, CDN or asset download. A copy is generated here as \"'`index.html`. AI Hub sessions use its supplied transport and lifecycle; standalone local co-op needs no online service.\n\nMove with A/D or arrows; W/S climbs or ducks. Space jumps, J/left-click chops, Q/right-click redirects, E deliberately enters a door or holds to rescue, Escape pauses. Standard gamepad: stick/D-pad, Cross jump, Square chop, R2 redirect, Circle/down duck, Triangle interact, Options pause. The native Controls screen supports rebinding. Touch: invisible left thumb movement/climb/down, right tap/hold jump, assisted chopping and a contextual action bubble.\n\nThe pause menu includes paged settings, help, About/feedback, Developer tools and standalone checkpoint/replay actions. Developer/practice/attract shifts cannot overwrite completed expedition records. Idle title menus start a real demonstration after ten seconds; waking input is consumed.\n\nBuild: `node tools/build.mjs`.\n\nVerify: `node tools/verify.mjs` (or `npm test`). This is a quiet aggregate with full gameplay/browser/Hub proof and may take several minutes. Uses the already-installed Python Playwright environment described in TASK.md; no browser installation is needed.\n\nAuthoring: `docs/authoring.md`. Research/provenance: `docs/research.md`, `docs/dependencies.md`. Verification and issue ledger: `docs/testing.md`, `docs/issues.json`. Network prediction/authority: `docs/network.md`. Original coded audio and native assets: `docs/audio.md`, `docs/assets.md`.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
