{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_179","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > ../PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n# Pick Axe Deplete — progress and handoff state\n\n## Deliverables\n\n- Development folder: \"'`Pick-Axe-Deplete-Pick-Axe-Pete-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-030126/`\n- Root game: `Pick-Axe-Deplete-Pick-Axe-Pete-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-030126.html`\n- Root feedback: `exit-interview.json`\n- Given plan/brief: `PLAN.md`, `TASK.md`\n- Title selected once from 50 riffs by actual `crypto.randomInt(50)` draw (index 20); config is `build-config.json`.\n\n## Current state — final verification running\n\nThe game is complete and bundled. Final source includes the last controller Options guard (root title/results must not disappear), explicit safe-transit/victory HUD, pointer-transparent touch hints, stable mouse rescue holds, touch action buffering, and owner-only network movement prediction. No further source edits are planned unless a release check fails.\n\nThe current verifier runs detached because a terminal session terminated the preceding long command. Its recorded PID is **1443043**; command `node tools/verify.mjs`, cwd is the development folder above. Read `docs/evidence/verify-process.json` and `verify-run.log` there. `tools/verify-background.mjs` launched this same quiet verifier with a recorded PID, detached process group and owned log. Do not launch a second copy while it runs.\n\nPoll the log/process and `docs/evidence/hub-progress.json`. Completion is `docs/evidence/verification.json` with `failures: []`, count **270**, and SHA-256 equal to the actual final root HTML. An older verification file exists, so check its hash/date against this run instead of trusting the filename alone. The wrapper'\"'s recorded start time distinguishes the current run. Stop only recorded owned processes if necessary; the Python harness closes its own OS-selected loopback server/browser in \"'`finally`.\n\n## Already verified\n\n- Native engine/handoff and Hub repositories match the plan: engine 0.89.1 at `8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691`; Hub client 1.4.0 at `35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869`.\n- Engine is unpatched. Released Hub client is pristine, first script after charset; hash `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a`.\n- 67 native checks pass: traversal/contact ordering, fairness, snapshots/RNG, tuning, 15 solo seed/route expeditions and 3 simultaneous couch expeditions. Normal inputs, no completion hacks.\n- 29 network checks pass, including 6 complete player-host/hidden-server expeditions over every route at 150 ms latency / 50 ms jitter / 5% loss. Local prediction changes traversal only; health, inventory, collisions, rewards and completion remain authoritative.\n- Browser input/audio suite has 41 cases. Before the final root-menu guard, all 41 passed, including real keyboard/mouse, standard pad stubs, all screens/rebinding/ownership, full expedition/replay, attract, actual CDP multitouch in both orientations, offline/live audio, and WebKit phone. Focused rebuilt mouse9 + portrait8 also passed. The same cases now additionally exercise title/nested/results Options and a complete second replay; case count stays 41.\n- Official Hub harness passed all 103 conformance/game assertions (1/2 players, faults, host leave, hidden server). A preceding complete aggregate passed **270 checks, zero failures**. Its actual lossy hidden-server round recorded both arcs, rescues, tools, keys, doors, 3 waves and victory with both miners alive; actual round wall time about 6 minutes versus a 15-minute limit.\n- Final guard'\"'s fresh standard-pad probe passed (\"'`Options` leaves title navigation visible). The current detached aggregate must certify the exact latest HTML.\n- Biome and Ruff are clean. JSON schema and all embedded script syntax/pristine dependency checks are in the aggregate.\n\n## Implementation and evidence\n\n- `src/content/`: validated tuning, room data, route personalities, `PD.PATTERNS` and `PD.EXTRACTION` data authoring.\n- `src/sim/mine.js`: seeded authority and ordered native traversal/action/rock/damage/pickup/door rules.\n- `src/input/`: native keyboard/pad, mouse/touch adapters and ordinary-input production Pilot.\n- `src/view/`: native 17-shape asset registry, equipment/11 poses, cave staging, lighting, HUD and Shell styling.\n- `src/audio/audio.js`: original native chip score, SFX and synthesized gibberish; independent buses, music default 0.1, no audio files.\n- `src/net/hub.js`: bounded authenticated transport, edge contexts/acks, interpolation and isolated native local movement prediction.\n- `src/main.js`: standalone/co-op/Hub lifecycles, paged menus/settings/About, Developer tools, checkpoints, attract and cleanup.\n- `tools/build.mjs`: exact single-file bundle + dev index + root feedback from `docs/feedback.json`.\n- `tools/verify.mjs`: one quiet command; 23 static + 67 simulation + 29 network + 41 browser + 110 Hub = 270 cases.\n- `tools/capture-evidence.py`: normal-input visual capture; owned browser closes after capture.\n- `docs/testing.md` and `issues.json`: **23 unique fixed issues, 9 critical**, including explicitly identified automated, visual and review findings. All feedback locations use this same count/model.\n- `docs/evidence/`: TV title/opening/unarmed/midgame/doorway/finale/reduced-motion/results/pause/Developer/About; portrait/landscape/WebKit; Hub and final verification JSON. Static menu captures finish CSS animations. Final doorway capture shows safe passage without stale key prompts.\n- Research: original manual and archive screenshots consulted; supplied 1982 review URL returned 404; original exact audio unknown. No original recorded art/audio is in the game.\n\n## Remaining work\n\n1. Wait for current PID 1443043 to complete; inspect only failures if any. Do not change source while verifying.\n2. Confirm final verification hash, JSON arrays (4/6/4), exact filename, root/dev bundle equality, and no remaining owned browser/server processes.\n3. Add final passing count/hash to docs/testing.md/PROGRESS.md (documentation only; do not rebuild/change game after a passing final artifact).\n4. Final reply must link the HTML and feedback and include **Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback**, in the task'\"'s question order. \"'`usage` is exactly `added on import`; model is OpenAI gpt-6.1-sol, max. Source Information includes date 2026-11-06 03:01:26, Pick Axe Pete (1982), PLAN.md, side-on arcade platformer, actual versions/native art/animation/coded audio, solo/local co-op/Hub co-op, research/testing/environment, and unknown original sound. Mention physical controller/real iOS/TV/listening stand-ins honestly.\n\n## Constraints\n\nAll new files stay under this work directory. Neighboring runs share ports/processes; do not inspect or alter them. Servers bind 127.0.0.1 on OS-selected ports. Stop only owned recorded PIDs. No TODOs/stubs or publication/approval step. All subagents completed their bounded work and closed their browsers. No external app messages were sent.\nEOF\ncat docs/evidence/verify-process.json && cat docs/evidence/verify-run.log'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_179","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > ../PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n# Pick Axe Deplete — progress and handoff state\n\n## Deliverables\n\n- Development folder: \"'`Pick-Axe-Deplete-Pick-Axe-Pete-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-030126/`\n- Root game: `Pick-Axe-Deplete-Pick-Axe-Pete-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-030126.html`\n- Root feedback: `exit-interview.json`\n- Given plan/brief: `PLAN.md`, `TASK.md`\n- Title selected once from 50 riffs by actual `crypto.randomInt(50)` draw (index 20); config is `build-config.json`.\n\n## Current state — final verification running\n\nThe game is complete and bundled. Final source includes the last controller Options guard (root title/results must not disappear), explicit safe-transit/victory HUD, pointer-transparent touch hints, stable mouse rescue holds, touch action buffering, and owner-only network movement prediction. No further source edits are planned unless a release check fails.\n\nThe current verifier runs detached because a terminal session terminated the preceding long command. Its recorded PID is **1443043**; command `node tools/verify.mjs`, cwd is the development folder above. Read `docs/evidence/verify-process.json` and `verify-run.log` there. `tools/verify-background.mjs` launched this same quiet verifier with a recorded PID, detached process group and owned log. Do not launch a second copy while it runs.\n\nPoll the log/process and `docs/evidence/hub-progress.json`. Completion is `docs/evidence/verification.json` with `failures: []`, count **270**, and SHA-256 equal to the actual final root HTML. An older verification file exists, so check its hash/date against this run instead of trusting the filename alone. The wrapper'\"'s recorded start time distinguishes the current run. Stop only recorded owned processes if necessary; the Python harness closes its own OS-selected loopback server/browser in \"'`finally`.\n\n## Already verified\n\n- Native engine/handoff and