ities, `PD.PATTERNS` and `PD.EXTRACTION` data authoring.\n- `src/sim/mine.js`: seeded authority and ordered native traversal/action/rock/damage/pickup/door rules.\n- `src/input/`: native keyboard/pad, mouse/touch adapters and ordinary-input production Pilot.\n- `src/view/`: native 17-shape asset registry, equipment/11 poses, cave staging, lighting, HUD and Shell styling.\n- `src/audio/audio.js`: original native chip score, SFX and synthesized gibberish; independent buses, music default 0.1, no audio files.\n- `src/net/hub.js`: bounded authenticated transport, edge contexts/acks, interpolation and isolated native local movement prediction.\n- `src/main.js`: standalone/co-op/Hub lifecycles, paged menus/settings/About, Developer tools, checkpoints, attract and cleanup.\n- `tools/build.mjs`: exact single-file bundle + dev index + root feedback from `docs/feedback.json`.\n- `tools/verify.mjs`: one quiet command; 23 static + 67 simulation + 29 network + 41 browser + 110 Hub = 270 cases.\n- `tools/capture-evidence.py`: normal-input visual capture; owned browser closes after capture.\n- `docs/testing.md` and `issues.json`: **23 unique fixed issues, 9 critical**, including explicitly identified automated, visual and review findings. All feedback locations use this same count/model.\n- `docs/evidence/`: TV title/opening/unarmed/midgame/doorway/finale/reduced-motion/results/pause/Developer/About; portrait/landscape/WebKit; Hub and final verification JSON. Static menu captures finish CSS animations. Final doorway capture shows safe passage without stale key prompts.\n- Research: original manual and archive screenshots consulted; supplied 1982 review URL returned 404; original exact audio unknown. No original recorded art/audio is in the game.\n\n## Remaining work\n\n1. Wait for current PID 1443043 to complete; inspect only failures if any. Do not change source while verifying.\n2. Confirm final verification hash, JSON arrays (4/6/4), exact filename, root/dev bundle equality, and no remaining owned browser/server processes.\n3. Add final passing count/hash to docs/testing.md/PROGRESS.md (documentation only; do not rebuild/change game after a passing final artifact).\n4. Final reply must link the HTML and feedback and include **Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback**, in the task'\"'s question order. \"'`usage` is exactly `added on import`; model is OpenAI gpt-6.1-sol, max. Source Information includes date 2026-11-06 03:01:26, Pick Axe Pete (1982), PLAN.md, side-on arcade platformer, actual versions/native art/animation/coded audio, solo/local co-op/Hub co-op, research/testing/environment, and unknown original sound. Mention physical controller/real iOS/TV/listening stand-ins honestly.\n\n## Constraints\n\nAll new files stay under this work directory. Neighboring runs share ports/processes; do not inspect or alter them. Servers bind 127.0.0.1 on OS-selected ports. Stop only owned recorded PIDs. No TODOs/stubs or publication/approval step. All subagents completed their bounded work and closed their browsers. No external app messages were sent.\nEOF\ncat docs/evidence/verify-process.json && cat docs/evidence/verify-run.log'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"pid\": 1443043,\n  \"started\": \"2026-11-06T11:48:33.823Z\",\n  \"command\": \"node tools/verify.mjs\",\n  \"cwd\": \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261106-030126__x7456b9/work/Pick-Axe-Deplete-Pick-Axe-Pete-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-030126\",\n  \"log\": \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261106-030126__x7456b9/work/Pick-Axe-Deplete-Pick-Axe-Pete-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-030126/docs/evidence/verify-run.log\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
