{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_187","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> docs/testing.md <<'EOF'\n\nThe long browser network proof disables canvas painting and HUD refresh on its two client copies, while retaining the real native tick loop, owner prediction, ordinary Pilot input, official Hub messages and wall-clock deadline. Actual canvas rendering is covered in the independent file-browser/full-expedition suite and visual captures. This keeps three same-process software-rendered copies from distorting the input/network timing test. A legal AI-team wipe in an earlier painted run was correctly reported as a loss; no health, supplies, simulation rules, tick rate or completion assertions were relaxed.\nEOF\nruff check tests/hub-browser.py && ruff format tests/hub-browser.py && node tools/verify-background.mjs\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
